\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 4-Suspected  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  leaves NZ dollar little changed   \b0\par\par\uc2 By Gyles Beckford and Kazunori Takada   \par \uc2 771 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Juni 2007\par 23:51\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Updates with latest market prices)   \par \par \uc2 WELLINGTON, June 18 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the second time in a week on Monday to push down its high-yielding \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  <NZD=>, traders said, but that did little to depress demand and most of the losses were quickly recovered.   \par \par \uc2 A spokeswoman at the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  (RBNZ) declined to say whether it had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  again -- after last week's first \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  since the \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar was floated in 1985 -- but traders said it had sold the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 The RBNZ said last week it had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  because the kiwi was at unjustifiably high, exceptional levels. It is concerned the high exchange rate could add to the pressure on some export sectors and push up the huge current account deficit.   \par \par \uc2 The kiwi dollar initially fell half a cent to a low of around $0.75, but it had recovered to around $0.7541/45 by 0400 GMT.   \par \par \uc2 "The market is getting its head around the fact that the RBNZ is not trying to get the massive shift lower in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but just keeping it pinned on the top side," said Sue Trinh, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at  \uc2 RBC Capital Markets.\par \par \uc2 The New Zealand dollar also fell half a yen to around 92.60 yen in the wake of the reported \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  but here, too, the effect was short-lived and it rallied to 93.09/25 yen <NZDJPY=R>, in sight of a 20-year high of 93.25 yen hit on Friday.   \par \par \uc2 On the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's preferred trade-weighted basis, the kiwi was at 73.57 <=NZD> after sliding as low as 73.20. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  forecast this month the trade-weighted index would average 70.2 in the first half of 2007 and 72 in the second half.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had stepped in on June 11 after the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hit a post-float high of $0.7640 following a surprise New Zealand interest rate rise to 8 percent on June 7.   \par \par \uc2 CONTINUED ACTION SEEN   \par \par \uc2 New Zealand's interest rates -- the highest in the industrial world -- have attracted inflows in the so-called carry trade, when investors borrow in low-yielding \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , such as the yen, to invest in high-yielding ones.   \par \par \uc2 Over the past year, the kiwi has risen nearly 20 percent against the U.S. dollar while the Australian dollar <AUD=>, which earlier in the month hit an 18-year high on expectations of higher interest rates, has gained around 12.5 percent.   \par \par \uc2 Traders said Monday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was about half of the suspected NZ$300-NZ$500 million ($225 million-$376 million) the Reserve Bank sold last week.   \par \par \uc2 The kiwi dollar spent much of last week in a range from $0.7450-$0.7510 after the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but it resumed its move higher on Friday after the Bank of Japan kept interest rates steady and U.S. data showed benign inflation pressures.   \par \par \uc2 "I think one of the key lessons out of this is that the market shouldn't get too hung up about there being some sort of line in the sand that the Reserve Bank is trying to defend," said Nick Tuffley, chief economist at ASB Bank.   \par \par \uc2 "It's giving us the signal that they are prepared to come in every now and then when there is a bit of a lift in the New Zealand dollar for reasons that are not much to do with New Zealand."   \par \par \uc2 The Reserve Bank can spend as much as it wants in kiwi-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  but it can only book losses up to NZ$1 billion on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market under an agreement with the government.   \par \par \uc2 Given the constraint, analysts estimate the RBNZ could spend around NZ$10 billion on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  -- just a fraction of the 35 trillion yen ($283 billion) the Japanese authorities sold in 2003 and 2004 when trying to prevent a rapid rise in the yen from damaging a fragile economy.   \par \par \uc2 It has previously said it would step in if the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was at exceptional levels not justified by economic fundamentals, if the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  could be expected to succeed and if it was consistent with its goal of achieving price stability.   \par \par \uc2 It has also said it would not try to go against the market trend and would be more likely to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in times when there was a disorderly market. ($1=NZ$1.33) ($1=123.5 yen)   \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 -NZDOLLAR (UPDATE 4)|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|AUF|ND|RNP|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070617e36h000n6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
