\par\par \b \uc2 NZ Shares End Higher; Cautious Trade As NZD, Rates Weigh   \b0\par\par\uc2 492 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Juni 2007\par 07:17\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 WELLINGTON (Dow Jones)--New Zealand shares closed higher on light volume Friday in a cautious response to rallying offshore markets, although brokers say the local bourse will struggle to make further gains from here as the country's high interest rates and strong New Zealand dollar continue to weigh.   \par \par \uc2 "A lot of investors are saying the Reserve Bank of New Zealand is going to win this battle (against domestic inflation pressures)... which will lead to a slowdown in the economy and won't be good for most companies," Hamilton Hindin Greene partner Grant Williamson said.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  raised rates three times and by a combined 75 basis points between March and June to the current 8.00%. The country's high yields have in turn supported a strong \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar exchange rate, which, despite RBNZ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to sell down the unit earlier this week, is still trading around US$0.7500, just shy of recent 25 year peaks.   \par \par \uc2 The NZX-50 closed up 19 points, or 0.5%, at 4212.46 on modest volume valued at NZ$83 million.   \par \par \uc2 ABN AMRO Craigs adviser Alexandra Dalzell said the high interest rates and \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , along with signs of a slowdown in retail sales, are likely to keep investors on the sidelines near term.   \par \par \uc2 "There's not a lot of new money coming into the market at the moment," Dalzell said.   \par \par \uc2 Among the gainers, Auckland International Airport rose 3% to NZ$2.82 as  \uc2 Macquarie Airports\uc2 ' sale of its stake in Rome-based Aeroporti di Roma refreshed talk the Australian airport investor may be considering a takeover play for Auckland Airport.   \par \par \uc2 Brokers said the deal may have trouble getting past Auckland Airport's local government majority shareholder, however.   \par \par \uc2 Defensive play  \uc2 Contact Energy\uc2  rose 0.6% to NZ$8.82, though it is still well off recent highs.   \par \par \uc2 Discount retailer The Warehouse rose 0.2% to NZ$5.98 after Australian grocer  \uc2 Woolworths Ltd.\uc2  lodged an appeal against a ruling by New Zealand's competition regulator barring it from bidding for Warehouse.   \par \par \uc2 Hamilton Hindin Greene's Williamson expects rival supermarket operator Foodstuffs Ltd. to follow suit, keeping the prospect of a contested bidding process alive. Still, he thinks Friday's move was widely anticipated by the market, so it is unlikely to boost the stock beyond current levels near term - especially given the high court appeal will be a "drawn out" affair.   \par \par \uc2 Bellwether Telecom Corp. closed steady at NZ$4.62 as it awaits an announcement on a successor for Chief Executive Theresa Gattung, who will leave the company June 30.   \par \par \uc2 Exporters Pumpkin Patch and Rakon gave back some of their recent gains on profit-taking, closing down 0.3% at NZ$3.70 and 0.6% at NZ$5.22, respectively.   \par \par \uc2 -By Rachel Pannett, Dow Jones Newswires; 64-4-471-5990; rachel.pannett@dowjones.com [ 15-06-07 0517GMT ]   \par \par \uc2 20712 5028 55118   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020070615e36f0004r\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
