\par\par \b \uc2 NZ dollar gains on renewed demand for yield   \b0\par\par\uc2 415 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Juni 2007\par 23:07\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 WELLINGTON, June 15 (Reuters) - The New Zealand dollar <NZD=> firmed on Friday as a rebound in global share markets lifted investors' risk appetite, sparking fresh demand for high-yielding \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 The klwi shrugged off data suggesting the housing market -- the main inflationary concern for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  -- was showing signs of cooling down following interest rate rises by the Reserve Bank of New Zealand. For story, click on [nWEL89185].   \par \par \uc2 Some analysts said the latest survey by the Real Estate Institute of New Zealand (REINZ) supported expectations that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will not raise rates again, but others said it was still to rule out the possibility of a further tightening.   \par \par \uc2 "It is perhaps too early to expect strong evidence of a turn in the housing market in response to higher interest rates delivered in March and April, and is inconclusive for the Reserve Bank," analysts at ANZ-National Bank said in a note to clients.   \par \par \uc2 At 0510 GMT the kiwi was at $0.7514/24, up from $0.7507/10 in late local trading on Thursday.   \par \par \uc2 Against the yen, it was also firmer at 92.41/55 yen <NZDJPY=R> against 92.10/22. The Bank of Japan kept interest rates on hold at 0.5 percent as expected on Friday.   \par \par \uc2 The market remained cautious of pushing the \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar too far up after the RBNZ's surprise \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Monday.   \par \par \uc2 Many players expect the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to step in again if the the kiwi, which the bank described as being exceptionally and unjustifiably high, firms towards its pre-\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  peaks.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar was trading just below a post float 22-year high of $0.7640 when the RBNZ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 Other data showed \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  manufacturing sales rebounded a seasonally adjusted 0.8 percent in the first quarter, supporting views the economy likely grew at a faster pace during the quarter.   \par \par \uc2 The manufacturing data is seen as the last piece of relevant data before gross domestic product for the first quarter is released on June 29.   \par \par \uc2 A Reuters poll preliminary median forecast is for GDP growth of 1 percent on the previous quarter.   \par \par \uc2 The benchmark NZ December 2017 bond <NZG1217=RNZL> ended flat at 6.84 percent, but outperformed U.S. and Australian bonds which both saw yields rise ahead of U.S. inflation data.   \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-NEWZEALAND-DOLLAR (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|ND|ABX|RBN|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070617e36e000mj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
