\par\par \b \uc2 CHARTING ASIA: NZ  \highlight22\uc2 Currency \highlight\uc2  May Resume Fall Vs Dollar   \b0\par\par\uc2 443 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Juni 2007\par 05:18\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By Jerry Tan \par  \par    A Dow Jones Newswires Column \par     \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--The Reserve Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 New Zealand\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's unprecedented \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Monday, which knocked the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 New Zealand\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dollar from its post-float high, has triggered negative signals for the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's technical outlook.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 The kiwi, as the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is known, could fall to US$0.7363 and possibly US$0.7236 in the near term, the charts indicate.   \par \par \uc2 At 0258 GMT Thursday, the New Zealand dollar was quoted at US$0.7500, having drifted between US$0.7451 and US$0.7540 since the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and below its post-float high of US$0.7638 set last Friday.   \par \par \uc2 Adding to the deteriorating outlook, data issued earlier Thursday showed a surprise 1.2% fall in retail sales in April, which is the steepest monthly decline in more than three years.   \par \par \uc2 The weak data could encourage expectations that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may stop tightening monetary policy. New Zealand's high interest rates and, in particular, the large gap between these rates and interest rates elsewhere, has been the main factor for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's gains over the past 12 months. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  hiked its official cash rate to a high of 8.00% on June 7.   \par \par \uc2 The threat of further \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has discouraged market participants from buying the kiwi, as the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is known.   \par \par \uc2 On the daily Kiwi-dollar chart, the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pair is trading within a flag formation between US$0.7451 and US$0.7540.   \par \par \uc2 The flag, which is a continuation pattern and usually marks the halfway point of a sharp move, warns of risk to the downside after the current consolidation ends.   \par \par \uc2 Adding the negative kiwi-dollar outlook is the slow stochastic indicator, which is bearish and falling from an overbought level. Since it is still far from oversold, there is room for the kiwi to fall further against the dollar near-term.   \par \par \uc2 The Moving Average Convergence/Divergence, or MACD, indicator is still in bullish mode. But the positive MACD histogram bars are contracting, which points to waning upward momentum of the short-term kiwi-dollar uptrend which started from the May 25 low of US$0.7236.   \par \par \uc2 The immediate target for the bearish kiwi-dollar outlook is US$0.7363, which is the measured objective of the flag formation. Any extension of the fall would target US$0.7236, the May 25 low.   \par \par \uc2 Any violation of the US$0.7638 resistance would abort the negative kiwi outlook.   \par \par \uc2 -By Jerry Tan, Dow Jones Newswires; 65-6415-4046; jerry.tan@dowjones.com   \par \par \uc2 -Edited by Iain McDonald [ 14-06-07 0318GMT ]   \par \par \uc2 1181   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020070614e36e00034\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
