\par\par \b \uc2 NZ manufacturing activity growth speeds up in May   \b0\par\par\uc2 354 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Juni 2007\par 02:02\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 WELLINGTON, June 14 (Reuters) - New Zealand manufacturing activity accelerated in May as new orders remained strong and offset the negative impact from a strong local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , a survey showed on Thursday.   \par \par \uc2 The seasonally adjusted Business NZ Performance of Manufacturing Index (PMI) rose to 56.8 last month from 54.4 in April, but was down from 58.1 in May last year.   \par \par \uc2 A figure over 50 indicates manufacturing is expanding, while under 50 indicates contraction.   \par \par \uc2 "The high dollar is still the hot issue, but the continued growth in new orders augurs well for future growth prospects," Business NZ economist John Pask said in a statement.   \par \par \uc2 Four of the PMI's five sub-indices rose on the previous month, with product and finished stocks showing the strongest gains. Deliveries was the only measure to decline from April.   \par \par \uc2 Pask said the strength of the New Zealand dollar was the most-mentioned negative factor facing manufacturers, but rising interest rates were also singled out along with signs of slowing demand, and a shortage of skilled labour.   \par \par \uc2 The New Zealand dollar <NZD=> hit a 22-year post-float high of $0.7640 last Friday, supported by New Zealand's high interest rates.   \par \par \uc2 However, the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Monday for the first time since the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  floated in 1985 to bring down what it regarded as an unjustifiably high NZ dollar.   \par \par \uc2 The kiwi has settled lower at around $0.7500 since the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 A rise in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  makes \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2 's exports less competitive on world markets, although it also lowers the price of imported raw materials.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  last week unexpectedly raised its official cash rate to 8 percent to curb medium-term inflation pressures generated by a hot housing market and resilient domestic consumption.   \par \par \uc2 A Reuters poll has only three of 16 forecasters expecting a further rate rise, although the median risk of a rise in July was put at 40 percent.   \par \par \uc2 NEWZEALAND-ECONOMY/PMI|LANGEN|ND|ABN|D|E|RBN|M|ABX|RNP|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070614e36e0000c\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
