\par\par \b \uc2 NZ dollar claws back after slipping on soft data   \b0\par\par\uc2 377 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Juni 2007\par 22:56\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 WELLINGTON, June 14 (Reuters) - The New Zealand dollar <NZD=> hovered around $0.75 on Thursday, recovering earlier losses suffered on weaker-than-expected retail sales data, though the market remained wary of further \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 The kiwi dropped nearly half a U.S. cent after data showed retail sales fell 1.2 percent in April, the biggest monthly drop in over three years, cooling expectations the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would raise interest rates again.   \par \par \uc2 But the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  regained its footing and gradually ground higher, supported by strength against the Aussie dollar.   \par \par \uc2 Analysts said the main focus of the market remained on the possibility of another \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  stepped into the market for the first time in over two decades on Monday.   \par \par \uc2 "I don't expect the RBNZ to be looking at \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  imminently again," said Sue Trinh, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at  \uc2 RBC Capital Markets.\par \par \uc2 "But if the exchange rate starts creeping higher, then we'd be urging a bit of caution."   \par \par \uc2 Trinh said the RBNZ could \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  if the kiwi's trade weighted index (TWI) rose to around 74.00/25 <=NZD>, a level where it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Monday.   \par \par \uc2 At 0510 GMT the kiwi was at $0.7507/10 little changed from $0.7500/03 in late local trading on Wednesday.   \par \par \uc2 On a trade-weighted basis, the New Zealand dollar firmed to 73.35 from 73.22.   \par \par \uc2 Against the Aussie, it nudged up to A$0.8944/53 <NZDAUD=R> against A$0.8918/26 after comments from Reserve Bank of Australia Governor Glenn Stevens dampened expectations for a near-term interest rate rise.   \par \par \uc2 Stevens said softer short-term price pressures provided time to assess the need for higher interest rates.   \par \par \uc2 Some traders said Business NZ data showing manufacturing activity accelerating slightly in May also offered the New Zealand dollar some support.   \par \par \uc2 The benchmark NZ December 2017 bond <NZG1217=RNZL> ended 2 basis points lower at 6.83 percent, but lagged their U.S. and Australian counterparts on lingering concerns of another rate lift by the RBNZ.   \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-NEWZEALAND-DOLLAR (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|ND|ABX|RBN|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070616e36d000hu\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
