\par\par \b \uc2 NZ Dollar Ends Lower, Caught In A Tight Range; Bonds Fall   \b0\par\par\uc2 406 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Juni 2007\par 07:41\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                           Close        Change \par  NZD/USD                  0.7505       -0.0026 \par  NZD/AUD                  0.8922       unchanged \par  July 2009 Bond           7.355%       +4.0 bps \par  Dec 2017 Bond            6.855%       +6.0 bps \par  10-Year U.S. Spread      +159.5 bps   -6.0 bps \par  90-Day Bank Bill         8.35%        +1.0 bps \par     \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 WELLINGTON (Dow Jones)--The New Zealand dollar closed lower Wednesday against the greenback, moving within a tight range as the market continued to analyze the Reserve Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 New Zealand\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's recent \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and overnight developments in the U.S.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 John Clarke, director at Bancorp Treasury, said the market was "a little bit nervy" following a sharp rise in U.S. bond yields that pushed the U.S. dollar higher ahead of a run of economic data that could alter the interest rate outlook there.   \par \par \uc2 "(RBNZ governor Alan) Bollard's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is getting a bit of assistance from the high U.S. yields because they are giving support to the U.S. dollar," said Clarke.   \par \par \uc2 "That's probably the key to where we go in the near term."   \par \par \uc2 Clarke added that with sentiment on the greenback improving and the threat of further \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the RBNZ limiting potential gains by the Kiwi, the bias for the New Zealand dollar in the near term is to the downside.   \par \par \uc2 But dealers noted the Kiwi continues to find support from speculative players in Asia and could yet move higher, depending on U.S. dollar strength.   \par \par \uc2 The local unit rose to JPY91.73 from JPY91.65 Tuesday.   \par \par \uc2 The market will look to April retail sales figures for local leads Thursday, though the economic data won't show the impact of two of the RBNZ's three recent rate hikes.   \par \par \uc2 NZ government bonds and swaps were sold off in line with the sharp fall in U.S. Treasury prices.   \par \par \uc2 "We've been quite volatile in the last few weeks, and it looks set to continue with the U.S. whipping around and our own domestic data and the RBNZ adding to the volatility," said one local trader.   \par \par \uc2 He said there is still "some realignment" of expectations on whether the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  decreases the chance of future rate hikes.   \par \par \uc2 -By Symon Ross, Dow Jones Newswires; 64-4-471-5990; symon.ross@dowjones.com   \par \par \uc2 -Edited by Roger Ng [ 13-06-07 0541GMT ]   \par \par \uc2 1062 20711 4171   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020070613e36d0006h\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
