\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar rises vs euro for fifth straight session   \b0\par\par\uc2 635 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Juni 2007\par 02:45\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Recasts; updates prices)   \par \par \uc2 NEW YORK (Reuters) - The dollar rallied against the euro for the fifth consecutive session Tuesday to an 11-week high, according to Reuters data, as rising U.S. Treasury yields lured investors.   \par \par \uc2 With few major U.S. economic indicators on Tuesday, dealers stuck to buying dollars based on the recent advantage of U.S. government bond yields over other government debt, a trade some analysts said could be close to running its course even as the benchmark U.S. Treasury yield climbed to a five-year high.   \par \par \uc2 "The dollar's getting support from Treasury yields," said Ron Simpson, director of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  research at Action Economics in Tampa, Florida. "But we're waiting for U.S. retail sales, CPI and PPI later in the week which may determine the dollar's direction."   \par \par \uc2 In late afternoon trading, the euro was down 0.4 percent from late Monday at $1.3311, near its session low of 1.3309 -- the pair's lowest level since March 30.   \par \par \uc2 Against the Japanese yen, the dollar was little changed at 121.70 yen, near a 4-1/2-year high around 122.20 yen hit in January.   \par \par \uc2 The greenback also hit a 3-1/2-month high at 1.2431 Swiss francs while the dollar index touched a two-month peak.   \par \par \uc2 Expectations of a near-term cut in U.S. interest rates have faded, sending bond yields higher.   \par \par \uc2 This, coupled with continued concerns about inflationary pressures voiced by Federal Reserve policy-makers, has supported the dollar.   \par \par \uc2 Some analysts cautioned that views on the dollar could change, depending on what information is gleaned on Wednesday from the U.S. retail sales report for May. The U.S. producer price index for May will be released on Thursday, with the U.S. consumer price index for May released on Friday.   \par \par \uc2 Investors will also be watching the U.S. Treasury's semiannual Report on International Economic and Exchange Rate Policies on Wednesday, for any comments on China's yuan.   \par \par \uc2 The yuan on Tuesday posted its largest gain against the dollar since its July 2005 revaluation, rebounding from a three-day slide after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  set a much higher reference rate for the Chinese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 U.S. policy-makers have argued that China's managed \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy artificially weakens the yuan, favors Chinese exports and widens the U.S. trade gap. While the Treasury report is not expected to label China a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  manipulator, investors may remain cautious ahead of the report.   \par \par \uc2 Investors will also closely monitor the unveiling of a bill in the Senate on Wednesday that would allow the U.S. to impose penalties on countries setting their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  artificially low.   \par \par \uc2 PLAYING SAFE WITH KIWI   \par \par \uc2 The New Zealand dollar was down 0.1 percent against the U.S. dollar after the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market and weakened its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the first time since the kiwi was floated in 1985.   \par \par \uc2 The RBNZ's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has not dented investor focus on reaching for higher yields and rewarding \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  where interest rates are likely headed higher.   \par \par \uc2 Monday's RBNZ selling helped to drive the New Zealand dollar down as much as 2 percent to a low of $0.7461. On Tuesday, the New Zealand dollar was at US$0.7506, still up 6.6 percent in the year-to-date.   \par \par \uc2 With the focus on yields, sterling rose broadly after Bank of England Governor Mervyn King said UK rates may need to rise again if capacity pressures, pricing intentions and inflation expectations remain elevated. But the pound's gains were capped by slightly softer-than-expected May inflation data.   \par \par \uc2 The British pound edged up 0.3 percent to $1.9750 .   \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 9)|LANGEN|FUN   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070612e36c00011\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
