\par\par \b \uc2 NZ Dlr Ends Steady, Consolidates After RBNZ's  \highlight22\uc2 FX Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 551 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Juni 2007\par 07:14\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                           Close        Change \par  NZD/USD                  0.7531       -0.0005 \par  NZD/AUD                  0.8922       -0.0031 \par  July 2009 Bond           7.315%       -4.0 bps \par  Dec 2017 Bond            6.795%       +0.5 bp \par  10-Year U.S. Spread      +165.5 bps   +0.5 bp \par  90-Day Bank Bill         8.34%        +1.0 bp \par     \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 WELLINGTON (Dow Jones)--The New Zealand dollar closed slightly lower Tuesday, consolidating in a tight range as the market digested the Reserve Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 New Zealand\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market Monday.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 The Kiwi fell to a low of US$0.7466 in overnight trading from US$0.7627 just before the RBNZ moved to weaken the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 But it traded steadily just above US$0.7500 Tuesday.   \par \par \uc2 Sue Trinh, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at  \uc2 RBC Capital Markets\uc2 , tipped the Kiwi to trade sideways against the greenback overnight, noting there is little U.S. data due that could alter the current picture.   \par \par \uc2 She pegs initial support at US$0.7490, with the topside likely limited at US$0.7550 near term.   \par \par \uc2 "Having said that I wouldn't rule out a push to fresh technical highs eventually, not today or tomorrow but in coming weeks, especially with the risk the RBNZ has to tighten again," said Trinh.   \par \par \uc2 Dealers said there is a good chance of further \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  should the Kiwi approach its post-float high of US$0.7640, touched Friday.   \par \par \uc2 "A one-off move is definitely not going to stem the tide," said HSBC senior dealer Daniel Brdanovic, who added however that there is "quite a large risk" speculators will challenge the RBNZ over further \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 A government policy adviser told Dow Jones Newswires the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sees US$0.7600 as an area of concern, with anything above that at this stage in the current economic cycle as grounds for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 Dealers generally didn't think the RBNZ intended to trigger a sharp downside move and had achieved its goal of ironing out a peak in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  cycle.   \par \par \uc2 "They've managed to get the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  down on a trade-weighted index basis. I think it has stabilized things and put some of the crosses back into the middle of recent ranges," said Mike Hollows, director of trading at HIFX.   \par \par \uc2 He noted the Kiwi pulled back from A$0.9050 against its Australian counterpart to "more realistic" levels near A$0.8900.   \par \par \uc2 The New Zealand dollar closed at Y91.65, down from Y91.70 Monday, with good demand on dips still evident, dealers said.   \par \par \uc2 Government bonds rallied at the short end, while the interest rate swap market was also stronger.   \par \par \uc2 "This \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has probably caused some uncertainty in terms of future rate moves. It's made people less confident there's going to be another hike and maybe happier to buy fixed interest, either to receive on the swaps or buy bonds," said one trader.   \par \par \uc2 Another trader said the market was correcting last week's selloff after the RBNZ raised the Official Cash Rate to 8.0%, and would now wait for second-quarter data before any more big moves.   \par \par \uc2 -By Symon Ross, Dow Jones Newswires; 64-4-471-5990; symon.ross@dowjones.com   \par \par \uc2 -Edited by Mary de Wet [ 12-06-07 0514GMT ]   \par \par \uc2 1062 20711 4171   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020070612e36c000a5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
