\par\par \b \uc2 NZ dollar holds near 75 cents, RBNZ and data eyed   \b0\par\par\uc2 484 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Juni 2007\par 23:10\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 WELLINGTON, June 13 (Reuters) - The New Zealand dollar <NZD=> settled in a modest range against the U.S. dollar on Wednesday as investors remained wary of possible \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and waited for data that might influence future rate rises.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has stayed within a moderate range around $0.7500 since the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  surprised on Monday in an unprecedented \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to sell what it regarded as an overvalued \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 "The kiwi's not been allowed to stray too far, with bargain hunters looking to buy when it dips and people a shade nervous about going too high because the RBNZ may reappear," said a dealer.   \par \par \uc2 At 0515 GMT the kiwi was at $0.7500/03 from $0.7516/25 in late local trading on Tuesday. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traded a $0.7480-0.7513 range.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has found $0.7470/80 a solid support level so far, but has been seen as capped at $0.7540/50 in the near term.   \par \par \uc2 The kiwi was up around 0.6 percent against the yen <NZDJPY=R> as it benefited from a move higher by the U.S. dollar, which has been buoyed by a rise in bond yields.   \par \par \uc2 The kiwi and the neighbouring Aussie have gained as investors covered short positions after a drop in Asian stock markets failed to spark an unwind of carry trades.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  have been major beneficiaries of carry trades, where investors borrow in low yield \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  such as the yen to invest in high yielders.   \par \par \uc2 New Zealand retail sales data is due on Thursday, with expectations in a Reuters poll of a flat outcome for the month of April, with core sales excluding motor vehicles sales and services also expected to be flat. March month sales surprised with a seasonally adjusted 1.3 percent rise.   \par \par \uc2 The strength of domestic consumption has been a factor in the RBNZ raising rates, which in turn has spurred the kiwi's appreciation.   \par \par \uc2 "The data covers the after the first two cash rate hikes, and so may yield the first indications of a softening in household consumption," said BNZ strategist Danica Hampton.   \par \par \uc2 Data on Wednesday showed New Zealand food prices rose 0.3 percent in May.   \par \par \uc2 New Zealand debt was weaker along the yield curve by as much as seven basis points as U.S. Treasuries recovered from an early slide that had sent yields up to a five-year high as upbeat economic data squashed expectations of a Federal Reserve rate cut.   \par \par \uc2 The benchmark NZ December 2017 bond <NZG1217=RNZL> ended seven basis points higher at 6.86 percent, but still outperformed U.S. and Australian counterparts on expectations that New Zealand rate rises may have come to an end.   \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-NEWZEALAND-DOLLAR (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|ND|ABX|RBN|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070615e36c001yu\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
