\par\par \b \uc2 ANALYSIS-NZ  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  to  \highlight22\uc2 intervene \highlight\uc2  again - but lightly   \b0\par\par\uc2 By Kazunori Takada   \par \uc2 708 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Juni 2007\par 08:19\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 WELLINGTON, June 12 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is expected to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  again to weaken the kiwi dollar, but not risk an all-out war against speculators because of its shoestring budget.   \par \par \uc2 The Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  (RBNZ), which on Monday used its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  powers for the first time since the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was floated in 1985, is unlikely to draw a line and to defend a set level, a method previously used by the Bank of Japan, analysts said.   \par \par \uc2 "Having declared war on the New Zealand dollar \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, the RBNZ now has to play a smart 'hit-and-run' tactic to keep the markets guessing and make their attacks effective," said Roger Kerr, director of Asia-Pacific Risk Management.   \par \par \uc2 It's a juggling act because the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's main task -- reining in inflation -- has prompted it to raise interest rates to 8 percent, the highest in the industrialised world.   \par \par \uc2 Monday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  signals the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  thinks rates have peaked, some analysts believe, although the authority hasn't spelled that out.   \par \par \uc2 Even without further hikes, the yield on the kiwi is big enough to keep attracting so-called carry trade, where investors borrow low-yielding \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , such as the yen, to fund the purchase of high-yielding assets, such as the New Zealand dollar.   \par \par \uc2 It's tough to stem that flow, certainly with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's limited \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  budget, analysts said.   \par \par \uc2 LIMITS   \par \par \uc2 Westpac Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist Michael Gordon estimates the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could spend around NZ$10 billion on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , just a fraction of the 35 trillion yen ($288 billion) the BOJ sold in 2003 and 2004 in trying to prevent the rapid rise in the yen from damaging the then-fragile economy.   \par \par \uc2 "If a George Soros look-alike wanted to take the RBNZ on, they just keep buying NZDs until the RBNZ runs out of selling resources," Kerr said.   \par \par \uc2 Soros is a hedge fund manager who pocketed more than $1 billion after he out-muscled the Bank of England in its defence of a weakening sterling.   \par \par \uc2 Traders speculate the RBNZ sold around NZ$300-NZ$500 million ($225-$376 million) against the U.S. dollar and possibly the yen, which sent the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  tumbling as much as 2 percent from just below the 22-year post float high of $0.7640.   \par \par \uc2 The Reserve Bank can only book losses up to NZ$1 billion on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market under an agreement with the government.   \par \par \uc2 The New Zealand dollar has so far stabilised around $0.75 <NZD=>, down over one U.S. cent from a 22-year peak on Friday, but still up more than 19 percent from a year earlier.   \par \par \uc2 CARRY TRADE   \par \par \uc2 Some economists think the RBNZ will aim to smooth the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rise, in a similar way to the Reserve Bank of Australia (RBA).   \par \par \uc2 The RBA has not officially \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  since 2001, when it supported the Aussie dollar when it fell to 50 U.S. cents <AUD=>. But it regularly buys and sells the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  -- it has sold over A$1 billion during the first four months of this year.   \par \par \uc2 But even a flexible approach could prove to be in vain given the power of the carry trade.   \par \par \uc2 "If the economy remains strong and they continue to tighten policy in response, and commodity prices continue to rise, it's difficult to see why the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  won't go higher," said  \uc2 Deutsche Bank\uc2  chief economist Darren Gibbs.   \par \par \uc2 Many analysts had expected any \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to come after it had finished raising rates because it had previously said it would not try to go against the market trend when \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 On Monday, the Reserve Bank said the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  did not prejudge the future direction of monetary policy, but analysts said the action diluted the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's message that it was still worried about inflation.   \par \par \uc2 "The market's conclusion after yesterday was that, if the bank is \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , then presumably we're close to the top in rates, if not at the top," Deutsche's Gibbs said.   \par \par \uc2 NEWZEALAND-DOLLAR/ (ANALYSIS)|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|ND|AUF|ABX|BNX   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070615e36c000eu\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
