ght22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the Reserve Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 New Zealand\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the previous session drove down the kiwi by nearly 2 percent.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 * The Aussie as well as the New Zealand dollar have both benefited from carry trades, where investors borrow in the low yielding Japanese yen to buy an asset bearing a higher return.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 * Shortly after midday, the Aussie dollar was quoted at $0.8433/38 versus $0.8421/26 here late on Friday, Reuters data showed. It traded in a $0.8427 to $0.8446 range so far.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 * The Aussie/kiwi pair <AUDNZD=R> was trading around $1.1234/45 rising from $1.1031 on Friday. The Aussie stayed firm against the yen <AUDJPY=R>, trading at 102.56/66 yen, up from 102.05/15 on Friday.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 * The Aussie soared to an 18-year high of $0.8476 last week after a slew of domestic economic reports prompted investors to price in a greater chance the Reserve Bank of Australia (RBA) will raise rates to 6.50 percent in the next few months.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 * Financial markets are now pricing in a 24 percent chance the RBA will raise the cash rate next month. That risk increases to 54 percent by August and 68 percent by September.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 * China's May inflation data came in bang in line with market expectations of a 3.4 percent rise. This was the highest in over two years, potentially giving the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  enough reason to tighten monetary policy.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 * Australian bond futures weak near recent lows with the global sell-off in debt markets showing no sign of abating as yet given surprising strength in world economic growth and expectations of rising official interest rates.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 * Eyes on U.S. 10-year yields to see if Friday's 5.25 percent peak is re-tested, which could easily come if this week's data on retail sales, producer prices and consumer prices are strong.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 * Local investors were wary ahead of a key speech by Reserve Bank of Australia Governor Glenn Stevens on Thursday, which could impact on growing expectations of a policy tightening here in the next few months.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 * Australian three-year bond futures <YTTc1> eased to 93.550, approaching last week's seven-year trough of 93.480. The 10-year bond contract <YTCc1> fell to 93.760, nearing a five-year low of 93.675.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-AUSTRALIA-BONDS/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 -NOON|LANGEN|Table|ABN|M|D|RBN|AUF|ABX|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070615e36c0004g\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
