\par\par \b \uc2 RPT- \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar firm, rising U.S. yields eyed for support   \b0\par\par\uc2 By Chikako Mogi   \par \uc2 637 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Juni 2007\par 07:43\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 TOKYO, June 12 (Reuters) - The dollar was steady against the yen and euro on Tuesday as investors focused on rising U.S. bond yields, while the New Zealand dollar inched up a day after the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 The market was closely watching whether benchmark 10-year U.S. Treasury yields would re-test last week's near five-year peak of 5.25 percent to determine how much further the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  could advance.   \par \par \uc2 Treasury yields have surged on diminishing expectations for Federal Reserve rate cuts and worries about more \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  monetary tightening around the world to combat inflation pressures, helping lift the dollar to a two-month high versus the euro.   \par \par \uc2 "There is a risk for yields to ease back after a rapid rise, but if upcoming data is strong, yields will likely come under upward pressure while the dollar may be supported," said Masafumi Yamamoto, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Nikko  \uc2 Citigroup.\par \par \uc2 The dollar was little changed around 121.65 yen hovering near the 4-1/2-year high of 122.20 yen struck in January.   \par \par \uc2 The euro was steady around $1.3363 near a two-month low around $1.3320 touched on Friday as the 10-year Treasury yield surged to match the Fed's target overnight rate of 5.25 percent. The euro edged up slightly to 162.60 yen   \par \par \uc2 The pound edged up after Bank of England Governor Mervyn King said late on Monday that British interest rates may need to rise again from the current 5.5 percent if signs of price pressures and capacity constraints stay high.   \par \par \uc2 Sterling was up 0.1 percent against the dollar at $1.9715   \par \par \uc2 With inflation concerns rising, analysts said they will be closely watching inflation data for Britain and the United States due out this week.   \par \par \uc2 British consumer price figures will be released at 0830 GMT on Tuesday. Core consumer prices are forecast to have risen 0.4 percent in May from the previous month and 3.3 percent year-on-year.   \par \par \uc2 "The dollar will be supported as long as the market sees rising interest rates reflecting firmness in the U.S. economy," said Masashi Kurabe, a senior manager of \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading at  \uc2 Bank of Tokyo-Mitsubishi\uc2  UFJ.   \par \par \uc2 "But if inflation picks up to push interest rates higher, that may end up causing a triple fall in stocks, bonds and the dollar," Kurabe said.   \par \par \uc2 LITTLE IMPACT ON CARRY   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to sell its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  after the kiwi hit a 22-year high versus the U.S. dollar last week has done little to cool carry trades, in which investors use low-yielding \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  such as the yen to pick up assets in high-yielding ones, traders said.   \par \par \uc2 Monday's RBNZ selling helped to drive the New Zealand dollar down as much as 2 percent to a low of $0.7467 The kiwi was up 0.1 percent at $0.7510, against $0.7640 on Friday -- the highest since the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was allowed to trade freely in 1985.   \par \par \uc2 New Zealand's action was seen as an isolated move with little overall market impact, as it ran counter to the trend of global monetary tightening in line with a solid global economy, traders said.   \par \par \uc2 The RBNZ raised rates to 8.0 percent last week, the highest in the industrialised world.   \par \par \uc2 "It was contradictory to sell the New Zealand dollar while tightening credit the previous week," Kurabe said. "But I see the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  as part of its smoothing \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The RBNZ has no intention of pushing the kiwi further down but may raise rates again due to inflation concerns." (Additional reporting by Tetsushi Kajimoto)   \par \par \uc2 LANGEN|GNN|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070612e36c000an\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
