\par\par \b \uc2 DJ Dollar In Ranges As  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Mkts Focus On New Zealand   \b0\par\par\uc2 629 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Juni 2007\par 15:03\par \uc2 Dow Jones Commodities Service\par \uc2 OSTDJ\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2007, Comtex News Network.  All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 NEW YORK, Jun 11, 2007 (DJCS via Comtex) --   \par \par \uc2 \f2 By Dan Molinski\par    Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 The dollar is in tight ranges against its top rivals early Monday, with \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets focused on New Zealand after its \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  stepped in overnight to curb the meteoric rise of its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 The Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  confirmed in a statement that it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to sell the \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar, the first time it's done so since it free-floated its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in 1985.   \par \par \uc2 "We regard current levels of the exchange rate as exceptional and unjustified in terms of the economic fundamentals," Reserve Bank Governor Alan Bollard said.   \par \par \uc2 The bank did not say how much it sold, though several traders said it appears the bank sold up to NZ$1.5 billion. The move knocked the New Zealand dollar to $0.7503 recently after it reached a 25-year high of about $0.7640 late Friday.   \par \par \uc2 In other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  early Monday, the euro was trading at $1.3348 from $1.3364 late Friday, while the dollar was at Y121.73 compared with Y121.75, according to EBS. The euro was at Y162.44 compared with Y162.67 late Friday. The dollar was at CHF1.2386 compared with CHF1.2359, while the U.K. pound traded at $1.9668 from $1.9678 late Friday.   \par \par \uc2 After the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , analysts are wondering who else may follow suit. Several \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are currently trading at multi-year highs against the generally weak U.S. dollar.   \par \par \uc2 Such \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  also raises questions about the profit-potential for carry trades, where investors borrow \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  that offer low interest rates, such as the yen, to buy those that pay high yields, such as the New Zealand dollar. Perhaps, analysts said, the trend by New Zealand and other high-yielding \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep offering even-higher rates will end.   \par \par \uc2 "Markets may well read [Monday's] move as the RBNZ showing a surprising degree of uncertainty, if not reluctance, to hike again," said analysts at Credit Suisse in an email. "A continuation of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would be clearly inconsistent with further rate hikes."   \par \par \uc2 The news out of New Zealand has shifted focus away from the U.S. dollar, which hit a two-month high against the euro on Friday after a sharp rise in U.S. bond yields boosted demand for the greenback.   \par \par \uc2 The rise in bond yields comes as investors continue to price out the now slim odds that the Federal Reserve will cut interest rates anytime this year. Improved U.S. economic data has swayed many economists away from the idea that rate cuts would be needed to help kick-start an economy that remains sluggish, partly due to a housing crunch.   \par \par \uc2 Overnight, Federal Reserve Bank of Cleveland President Sandra Pianalto said housing price adjustments have slowed U.S. economic growth, but said there has been no spill-over into the consumer sector yet.   \par \par \uc2 Still, she said at a conference in Dublin, a contagion effect remains a risk. "We are watching that very closely," she said.   \par \par \uc2 The dollar reacted little to Pianalto's comments, however, and stayed in tight ranges against the euro and yen.   \par \par \uc2 There is no important U.S. data report out Monday, and traders said the dollar is likely to trade mostly sideways ahead of a raft of U.S. economic data that will be released starting on Tuesday. Friday's consumer price inflation data will be a key report.   \par \par \uc2 -By Dan Molinski, Dow Jones Newswires; 201-938-2245; dan.molinski@dowjones.com   \par \par \uc2 (Shri Navaratnam in Wellington and Quentin Fottrell in Dublin contributed to this report.)   \par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires   \par \par \uc2 06-11-07 0902ET   \par \par \uc2 Dokument OSTDJ00020070611e36b00138\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
