\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar advances to 3-1/2-month high vs Swiss franc   \b0\par\par\uc2 653 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Juni 2007\par 02:40\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Recasts, updates prices)   \par \par \uc2 NEW YORK, June 11 (Reuters) - The dollar rallied to a 3-1/2 month high against the Swiss franc on Monday, with U.S. 10-year Treasury yields over 5 percent and investors largely ignoring the \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's first market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in 22 years.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar posted its largest decline in 15 months at one point after the Reserve Bank of New Zealand sold its own \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but there was only limited impact on carry trades in which investors buy high-yielding \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  like the New Zealand dollar funded by borrowing low-cost \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  such as the Swiss france or the Japanese yen.   \par \par \uc2 "Have the conditions for the carry trade altered? No," said Joe Trevisani, chief market analyst at \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  Solutions, in Saddle River, New Jersey. "Everyone is looking over their shoulder but for now we are still close enough to highs on the kiwi that if things calm down, it will go higher."   \par \par \uc2 The U.S. dollar briefly peaked just above 1.2400 Swiss francs <CHF=>, before settling at 1.2380 francs, up 0.3 percent from late Friday.   \par \par \uc2 The New Zealand dollar fell 1.7 percent to US$0.7510 <NZD=>, well off highs of US$0.7640 reached on Friday, the strongest level since the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was floated in 1985.   \par \par \uc2 The U.S. dollar climbed for the fourth consecutive session against the euro, with the euro down 0.1 percent at $1.3354 <EUR=>.   \par \par \uc2 The RBNZ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb the \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar came four days after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  surprised markets by raising its key interest rate to 8 percent, the highest benchmark rate in the industrialized world.   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is one of the biggest risks to carry trades, but the modest impact on the broader market showed the resilience of the seemingly ubiquitous trading strategy.   \par \par \uc2 "After months of warning, the action (by the RBNZ) backs up the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's stance," Camilla Sutton, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist with Scotia Capital in Toronto, wrote in a note.   \par \par \uc2 "Fall-on effects on carry have been evident, but remain somewhat muted. We would expect today's news to benefit the Australian dollar/New Zealand dollar cross ... ," she said.   \par \par \uc2 Against the yen, the New Zealand dollar tumbled 1.6 percent to 91.47 yen <NZDJPY=R>. The dollar was little changed against the yen at 121.74 yen <JPY=>.   \par \par \uc2 The spread of the implied benchmark U.S. interest rate in December 2008 over the euro zone equivalent was near its widest in three months, with fixed-income markets reflecting low implied chances that the Federal Reserve would have to loosen monetary policy this year or next.   \par \par \uc2 "We think that as a result of the repricing of the U.S. yield curve here and the capitulation in terms of U.S. growth deceleration ... the dollar deterioration is likely to pause over the very short term," Jack Malvey, chief global fixed income strategist with  \uc2 Lehman Brothers\uc2 , said at the Reuters Investment Outlook Summit.   \par \par \uc2 "But in a 12- to 18-month period we still envision the dollar to weaken particularly against Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ."   \par \par \uc2 With no major U.S. economic data on Monday, dealers kept liquid \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , other than the New Zealand dollar, in narrow ranges, waiting for the May U.S. retail sales report on Wednesday.   \par \par \uc2 Dealers said robust risk appetite, supported by gains in global equity markets, could mean buyers dip their toe back into the New Zealand dollar market later this week, barring any further action from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 The Australian dollar slipped 0.2 percent versus the U.S. dollar <AUD=> to US$0.8435, but it jumped 1.5 percent against the New Zealand dollar to NZ$1.1219 <AUDNZD=>.   \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 9)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|E|RBN|U|J|UKI|Z|CANT|AUF|RNP|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070611e36b00019\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
