\par\par \b \uc2 Aussie dlr supported by rate outlook, eyes cenbank   \b0\par\par\uc2 By Anirban Nag   \par \uc2 494 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Juni 2007\par 01:48\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  SYDNEY, June 12 (Reuters) - The Australian dollar nudged up on Tuesday, benefiting from speculation that domestic interest rates could rise in coming months, as well as firm commodity prices and a shift out of the New Zealand \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2  Fresh merger and acquisition news also underpinned the Aussie, which last week scaled a 18-year high of $0.8476 against the U.S. dollar.   \par \par \uc2  Late on Monday, Canada's  \uc2 Brookfield Asset Management Inc.\uc2   offered to buy construction and property firm  \uc2 Multiplex Group\uc2   in a deal worth A$4.2 billion.   \par \par \uc2  "In the short term, the M&A story, rising stock markets and commodities will continue to be supportive of the Aussie," said Robert Rennie, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at  \uc2 Westpac Banking Corp.\par \par \uc2  "But all eyes are on the Reserve Bank chief as it has been a while since we have heard something from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ."   \par \par \uc2  Governor Glenn Stevens speaks at a conference on Thursday and is expected to sound a hawkish note after a slew of strong economic data last week reignited concerns about price pressures. That could give a lift to the Aussie, analysts said.   \par \par \uc2  Financial markets are pricing in a 24 percent chance Australia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would lift rates here next month. That risk increases to 54 percent in August and 72 percent by September.   \par \par \uc2  At 4:00 p.m. (0600 GMT) the Aussie dollar <AUD=> was quoted at $0.8434/37, compared with $0.8421/26 here late on Friday, and after having eased a low of $0.8405 in offshore trade.   \par \par \uc2  It also rose against the New Zealand dollar <AUDNZD=R>, trading around $1.1208/19, rising from $1.1031 on Friday.   \par \par \uc2  The Aussie eased in the kiwi dollar's wake on Monday after \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  -- the first time it has taken such action since the kiwi was floated in 1985.   \par \par \uc2  However, analysts said if the Reserve Bank of New Zealand steps in again to curb the kiwi's strength it could see yield-hungry investors switch into the Aussie.   \par \par \uc2  "In an environment where carry trades are very much alive, and where the kiwi would have generally outperformed, the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  adds a two-sided risk in the short term," said John Kyriakopoulos, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at National Australia Bank.   \par \par \uc2  "The Aussie would benefit from this as we have already seen some of the switch happen from the kiwi to the Aussie."   \par \par \uc2  The Aussie as well as the New Zealand dollar have both benefited from carry trades, where investors borrow in the low yielding Japanese yen to buy an asset bearing a higher return.   \par \par \uc2  The kiwi <NZD=> steadied on Tuesday after falling nearly 2 percent on Monday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which traders speculated was worth between NZ$300 million and NZ$500 million.      \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-AUSTRALIA-DOLLAR (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|AUF|ABX|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070614e36b0029o\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
