\par\par \b \uc2 NZ dlr recovers some losses made on  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 519 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Juni 2007\par 23:24\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Adds analyst comments, updates price)   \par \par \uc2 WELLINGTON, June 12 (Reuters) - The New Zealand dollar <NZD=> recouped some of its losses on Tuesday, steadying after an unprecedented \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  the previous day had had sent it tumbling around 2 percent.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was little moved after a closely-watched speech by Reserve Bank of New Zealand Governor Alan Bollard to an agricultural group provided few surprises.   \par \par \uc2 "Some of the Asian accounts are starting to doubt whether or not the Reserve Bank has got any muscle, but I think it's more about a signalling effect than the weight of money behind the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Danica Hampton, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 At 0559 GMT the kiwi was at $0.7516/25, having traded a relatively narrow $0.7504-0.7527 range.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  fell as low as $0.7465 in post-New Zealand trade on Monday, pushed down also by a stronger U.S. dollar. It had been trading slightly below $0.7640, a 22-year post high hit on Friday, when the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 The RBNZ said it stepped into the market on Monday, for the first since the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was floated in 1985, because the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was at unjustifiable and exceptional levels.   \par \par \uc2 Traders speculate the RBNZ sold around NZ$300-NZ$500 million ($225-$376 million) of kiwi dollars against the U.S. dollar, and possibly the yen, halting the kiwi's meteoric rise following last week's interest rate rise.   \par \par \uc2 In his speech, Bollard made no mention of the level of the kiwi dollar but did warn that higher payouts to dairy farmers, fuelled by strong commodity prices, might add to an already-stretched economy.   \par \par \uc2 "To the extent that some of it is spent, it may make it harder to achieve our medium-term inflation target," Bollard said in speech notes.   \par \par \uc2 Analysts said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's hawkish monetary policy would continue to provide the kiwi with good support.   \par \par \uc2 "We still see risks skewed toward further RBNZ tightening in the third quarter, and unless the RBNZ is willing to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  on a sustained basis, the \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar will eventually push to fresh cyclical highs above 0.7640," said Sue Trinh, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at  \uc2 RBC Capital Markets.\par \par \uc2 Most players expect New Zealand's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to step into the market again, but did not expect a heavy-handed approach given the risks involved.   \par \par \uc2 "There's potential for the market to take the bank on here, and what if they keep bidding the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  up and up and up," said Bank of New Zealand senior economist Craig Ebert.   \par \par \uc2 "The bank could have picked a fight that it's going to be on the backfoot with. Time will tell."   \par \par \uc2 Last Friday, Bollard told Reuters in an interview that at least some of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's recent appreciation had been justified by the sharp rise in dairy prices, but he doubted the RBNZ's rate rises were responsible.   \par \par \uc