\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-NZ dollar settles after RBNZ  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 402 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Juni 2007\par 23:24\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Adds comment, updates price)   \par \par \uc2 WELLINGTON, June 12 (Reuters) - The NZ dollar <NZD=> sat just above $0.75 on Tuesday, as investors absorbed the Reserve Bank of NZ's unprecedented \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  of the previous day, which sent the kiwi tumbling around 2 percent.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (RBNZ) said it sold the kiwi on Monday -- for the first time since the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was floated in 1985 -- because the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was at unjustifiable and exceptional levels.   \par \par \uc2 The RBNZ's action halted the kiwi's meteoric rise following last week's interest rate hike, but the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's hawkish monetary policy was seen as still supporting the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rise.   \par \par \uc2 "We still see risks skewed toward further RBNZ tightening in the third quarter, and unless the RBNZ is willing to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  on a sustained basis, the \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar will eventually push to fresh cyclical highs above 0.7640," said Sue Trinh, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at  \uc2 RBC Capital Markets.\par \par \uc2 At 2330 GMT the kiwi was at $0.7504/14, having traded a narrow $0.7507-0.7512 range.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  touched an offshore low of $0.7467 in the wake of the RBNZ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and a stronger U.S. dollar. It had touched a high of $0.7640 on Friday, and was around $0.7630 when the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 Analysts said \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was in uncharted territory and was faced formidable challenges.   \par \par \uc2 "There's potential for the market to take the bank on here, and what if they keep bidding the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  up and up and up," said Bank of New Zealand senior economist Craig Ebert.   \par \par \uc2 "The bank could have picked a fight that it's going to be on the backfoot with. Time will tell."   \par \par \uc2 In the short term, resistance for the kiwi was seen at around $0.7560, above which the market may fear further \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 RBNZ governor Alan Bollard was due to speak to an agri-business group at 3.30 p.m. (0330 GMT) on the dairy industry and the New Zealand economy.   \par \par \uc2 Last Friday, Bollard told Reuters in an interview that at least some of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's recent appreciation had been justified by the sharp rise in dairy prices but he doubted the RBNZ's rate rises were responsible.   \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-NEWZEALAND-DOLLAR (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|ND|ABX|RBN|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070614e36b0025c\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
