\par\par \b \uc2 ANALYSTS VIEW 5-NZ dollar tumbles on RBNZ selling  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 1,342 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Juni 2007\par 08:26\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  TOKYO, June 11 (Reuters) - The \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar tumbled as much as 1.8 percent from near a 22-year peak against the U.S. dollar on Monday as \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to sell the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , calling its value exceptionally and unjustifiably high.   \par \par \uc2  The kiwi initially plunged on rumours of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  that the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  later confirmed, the first such \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  since the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  allowed the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to trade freely in 1985.  For the RBNZ's statement, click on [ID:nNZF000394].   \par \par \uc2  MARKET REACTION   \par \par \uc2  - The NZ dollar fell 1.8 percent to a low of $0.7497 and was last at $0.7500 <NZD=D4> compared with $0.7635 in late U.S. trade on Friday. The kiwi also fell more than 1 percent against the euro <EURNZD=R> and yen <NZDJPY=R>.   \par \par \uc2  - The kiwi jumped to a post-float peak of $0.7640 last Friday after the RBNZ surprised markets by raising interest rates last week to 8.0 percent, the highest in the industrialised world.   \par \par \uc2  - The Australian dollar shed 0.5 percent to $0.8416 <AUD=D4> on the kiwi's drop, but other major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were stable. The euro slipped 0.15 percent to $1.3352 <EUR=> from late U.S. trade Friday.   \par \par \uc2  COMMENTS   \par \par \uc2  (Following comments were made after RBNZ confirmation)   \par \par \uc2  ROBIN CLEMENTS, SENIOR ECONOMIST,  \uc2 UBS\uc2  NZ, CHRISTCHURCH   \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  capacity was described as adding another instrument to the monetary policy tool kit. Now the RBNZ has actually used it. But will the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  have a meaningful impact on the exchange rate? That is, was it opportune?   \par \par \uc2  "Presumably the RBNZ thought the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  today could be effective. As it stands the NZ dollar is down over 1 percent against the U.S. dollar, so the jury is out. Time will tell."   \par \par \uc2  - - - -   \par \par \uc2  KHOON GOH, SENIOR ECONOMIST, ANZ-NATIONAL BANK, WELLINGTON   \par \par \uc2  "Today's action shows they've lost patience with the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2  "It's not going to the send the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  into a bearish mode. I think what they (Reserve Bank) are trying to do is cut off the peaks of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . All they're doing is avoiding sending the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to the 78 U.S. cent level, which it looked destined for.   \par \par \uc2  "They will probably stop if they feel that the New Zealand dollar has fallen to a level where they feel comfortable with. If not, they will continue."   \par \par \uc2  - - - -   \par \par \uc2  STEPHEN TOPLIS, HEAD OF RESEARCH, BANK OF NEW ZEALAND, WELLINGTON   \par \par \uc2  "For the NZ dollar, it's all negative short term. But in the end, economic fundamentals will win the day. If domestic growth fails to wane and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  remains up against it on the inflation front, the NZ dollar will remain well-supported.   \par \par \uc2  "Even after today's correction, it should be noted that the NZ dollar is not far different from where it as immediately after the RBNZ's monetary policy statement."   \par \par \uc2  - - - -   \par \par \uc2  SUE TRINH, SENIOR \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCY\b0 \highlight\uc2  STRATEGIST, RBC CAPITAL MARKETS, SYDNEY   \par \par \uc2  "We have been surprised by this \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  since the RBNZ has previously outlined four necessary conditions for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and of the four conditions, there is one factor that put the odds of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the RBNZ as very low -- \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  would have to be consistent with Policy Targets Agreement (PTA) (i.e. the RBNZ's monetary policy objectives).   \par \par \uc2  "The RBNZ needs a high \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  given non-tradable inflation pressure, and any \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  risks causing a negative inflationary impact, which would be contrary to the PTA.   \par \par \uc2  "Late Friday, RBNZ's Governor Bollard said that New Zealand still had medium-term inflation to deal with.   \par \par \uc2  "This is the first time in the post float era that the RBNZ has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets. Without historical precedent, it will be difficult to judge how long the RBNZ will be in the market to weaken the NZD, and how much weaker NZD could go.   \par \par \uc2  "But the international evidence on successful \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is mixed, and \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is a distraction from the RBNZ's core policy objective, which is to contain medium-term inflation within 1-3 percent, where the most potent instrument is the OCR.   \par \par \uc2  "Lastly, the RBNZ has limited capital to play with (the RBNZ was given an additional NZ$1 billion for the specific purposes of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in 2004, and to absorb marked-to-market losses).   \par \par \uc2  "For these reasons, a cyclical top in NZD has yet to be put in place as long as the USD is weak, and the RBNZ is tightening. NZD/USD faces support at 0.7495.  Below there is more sturdy support at 0.7405."   \par \par \uc2  - - - -   \par \par \uc2  MASAKI FUKUI, SENIOR MARKET ECONOMIST, MIZUHO CORPORATE BANK, TOKYO   \par \par \uc2  "I do not think this will prompt a reversal of carry trades, although it will likely moderate the pace at which the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  appreciates. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  will keep on its firm trend and may even renew its high (against the yen).   \par \par \uc2  "The same goes for other high-yielding \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , although the Australian dollar was dragged down as well today ... The basic trend (of yen carry trades) has not changed.   \par \par \uc2  "That has much to do with Japanese investors buying higher-yielding \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , while foreign investors may bear in mind the need to reduce their carry trade positions amid growing uncertainty over equity markets and the global economy."   \par \par \uc2  - - - -   \par \par \uc2  (Following comments were made before RBNZ confirmation)   \par \par \uc2   KOJI FUKAYA, SENIOR \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCY\b0 \highlight\uc2  STRATEGIST, DEUTSCHE BANK, TOKYO   \par \par \uc2  "It would not surprise me if there was an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , given that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had made cautious comments on appreciation of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2   "It may impact other high-yielding \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  by unnerving investors conducting carry trade who have become wary about rising intererst rates worldwide.   \par \par \uc2  "That would prompt those investors to cover yen short positions against cross \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  such as the euro, rather than the dollar.   \par \par \uc2  "But such an adjustment will unlikely last long, as long as global economies stay in the current sound conditions.   \par \par \uc2  "Still, if an adjustment of overextended positions among investors drags on, the yen would appreciate, pushing euro/yen as low as 157-158 yen and dollar-yen to below 120 yen." - - - -   \par \par \uc2  MAGNUS PRIM, CHIEF ASIA \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCY\b0 \highlight\uc2  STRATEGIST, SEB, SINGAPORE   \par \par \uc2  "They are taking steps obviously. They are a bit concerned about the development we have seen for some time in the New Zealand dollar. But having said that, it's very hard for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  like this to turn the trend. The aim is not to turn the trend, the aim is to slow down the development we have seen."   \par \par \uc2  He did not expect the move to have any major impact on other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2  - - - -   \par \par \uc2  TOMOKO FUJII, HEAD OF ECONOMICS AND STRATEGY JAPAN, BANK OF AMERICA, TOKYO   \par \par \uc2  "There had been comments saying that the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  levels (of the New Zealand dollar) can't be justified by fundamentals. So it's not a big surprise that such rumours have emerged.   \par \par \uc2  "At the moment, it's an issue specific to the New Zealand dollar, although there could be some spillover.   \par \par \uc2  "I don't think there will be a direct impact on investor risk appetite just from what happened with the New Zealand dollar.   \par \par \uc2  "With regard to the yen, there will be a focus on investor risk appetite and on Chinese economic data due this week.   \par \par \uc2  "The situation seems alright but if equities fall more than investors can bear, there would be a risk of a steeper-than-expected reversal of yen carry trades."   \par \par \uc2  - - - -   \par \par \uc2  BACKGROUND   \par \par \uc2  - In the past two RBNZ policy statements, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has said the NZ dollar was exceptionally and unjustifiably high based on medium-term fundamentals, which some analysts had seen as signalling the potential risk of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2  - In an interview with Reuters last week, RBNZ Governor Alan Bollard said the kiwi was "high and hurting" and that he was not convinced New Zealand's steep short-term rates were pushing up the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  For interview highlights, click on [ID:nWEL14507]      \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 -NZDOLLAR (INSTANT, PICTURE, GRAPHIC)|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|U|AUF|J|ND   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070614e36b000do\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
