\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2-NZ  \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervenes \highlight\uc2 , sending kiwi sliding   \b0\par\par\uc2 By Kazunori Takada   \par \uc2 899 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Juni 2007\par 05:07\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Adds more analyst comment, background)   \par \par \uc2 WELLINGTON, June 11 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Monday for the first time in more than two decades to cap a soaring New Zealand dollar, spurring a 2 percent fall in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 Saying the kiwi dollar was unjustifiably high, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  entered the market to rein in a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  that had jumped 28 percent in the last year to hit a 22-year peak on Friday.   \par \par \uc2 "As stated in our June monetary policy statement, we regard current levels of the exchange rate as exceptional and unjustified in terms of the economic fundamentals," Alan Bollard, governor of the Reserve Bank of New Zealand, said in a statement.   \par \par \uc2 The kiwi slid to a session low of $0.7486 after the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , down from Friday's high of $0.7640. The neighbouring Australian dollar also fell.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's first \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  since the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was floated in 1985 came after a surprise interest rate hike to 8 percent last week to rein in inflation and the reappointment of Bollard for a second five-year term two weeks ago.   \par \par \uc2 New Zealand's high rates -- the highest in the industrial world -- have attracted inflows in the so-called carry trade, when investors borrow in low-yielding \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , such as the yen, to invest in high-yielding ones.   \par \par \uc2 The inflows helped push up the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  3.5 percent in the last month alone but analysts said the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was unlikely to turn the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  around.   \par \par \uc2 "Today's action shows they've lost patience with the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . It's not going to send the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  into a bearish mode. What they are trying to do is cut off the peaks of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Khoon Goh, senior economist at ANZ-National Bank.   \par \par \uc2 "All they're doing is avoiding sending the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to the 78 U.S. cent level, which it looked destined for."   \par \par \uc2 CARRY TRADES   \par \par \uc2 The New Zealand dollar also fell around 2 percent against the yen <NZDJPY=R> to about 91.13 yen, down from a 17-year high near 93 yen struck on Friday.   \par \par \uc2 "For the NZ dollar, it's all negative short term. But in the end, economic fundamentals will win the day," said Stephen Toplis, head of research at Bank of New Zealand. "If domestic growth fails to wane and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  remains up against it on the inflation front, the NZ dollar will remain well-supported."   \par \par \uc2 The Reserve Bank of NZ has had the power to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market since the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was floated in March 1985, but it had never used the power until Monday.   \par \par \uc2 The neighbouring Australian dollar <AUD=>, also a high-yielding \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , was caught in the sell-off and fell to a low around $0.8395 from $0.8430, before rebounding slightly. Australian financial markets were closed for a public holiday.   \par \par \uc2 "I do not think this will prompt a reversal of carry trades, although it will likely moderate the pace at which the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  appreciates. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  will keep on its firm trend and may even renew its high (against the yen)," said Masaki Fukui, senior market economist,  \uc2 Mizuho Corporate Bank\uc2  in Tokyo.   \par \par \uc2 "The same goes for other high-yielding \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , although the Australian dollar was dragged down as well today ... The basic trend (of yen carry trades) has not changed.   \par \par \uc2 KIWI STILL BULLISH   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had previously said it would only step in if the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was at exceptional levels not justified by economic fundamentals, if the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  could be expected to succeed, and if it was consistent with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's role of achieving price stability.   \par \par \uc2 It has also said it would not try to go against the market trend and would be more likely to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in times when there was a disorderly market.   \par \par \uc2 "Without historical precedent, it will be difficult to judge how long the RBNZ will be in the market to weaken the NZD, and how much weaker NZD could go," said Sue Trinh, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist,  \uc2 RBC Capital Markets\uc2  in Sydney,   \par \par \uc2 "But the international evidence on successful \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is mixed, and \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is a distraction from the RBNZ's core policy objective, which is to contain medium-term inflation within 1-3 percent, where the most potent instrument is the official cash rate."   \par \par \uc2 Bollard has described the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  as being exceptionally and unjustifiably high in the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's past two policy statements.   \par \par \uc2 Asked by Reuters on Friday if the comments were deliberately used to raise \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  as an issue, Bollard said: "We just want to be quite transparent about our view about the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and those are our views."   \par \par \uc2 In the same interview, he said some of the kiwi's rise was justified by high commodity prices and expressed doubt that the RBNZ's own rate rises were to blame.   \par \par \uc2 The RBNZ forecast in its June monetary policy statement the trade-weighted New Zealand dollar <=NZD> would average 68.6 in the first half of 2007 and 68.3 in the latter half.   \par \par \uc2 As of Monday it was at 73.45, below an all-time high of 74.54 reached in December 2005. (Additional reporting by Tokyo bureau)   \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 -NZDOLLAR (UPDATE 2,PICTURE,GRAPHICS)|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|ND|AUF|J|UKI|RNP|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070614e36b0004q\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw200\pich25\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3000\pichgoal375
