\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE:  \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand \highlight\uc2  Dollar Reverses Run On  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 1,118 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Juni 2007\par 22:48\par \uc2 Dow Jones Business News\par \uc2 DJON\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 By Wanfeng Zhou   \par \par \uc2 NEW YORK (Dow Jones) -- Less than a week after surprising the market with an interest-rate hike that boosted New Zealand's dollar to 22-year highs, the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  now find itself in a position to dampen the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rise.   \par \par \uc2 The Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  confirmed Monday that it had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market by selling the \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar to weaken it. It is the first time the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  since the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was floated in 1985.   \par \par \uc2 "As stated in our June Monetary Policy Statement, we regard current levels of the exchange rate as exceptional and unjustified in terms of the economic fundamentals," Reserve Bank Governor Alan Bollard said in a statement posted on the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's web site.   \par \par \uc2 The New Zealand dollar, or the kiwi, tumbled on Monday, falling 2% against the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , 1.7% against the Australian dollar, and 1.9% against the yen.   \par \par \uc2 "The unprecedented \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ...caught the market completely wrong-footed after last week's surprise rate hike," said Marc Chandler, global head of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategy at  \uc2 Brown Brothers Harriman.\uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  effectively reversed last [week]'s strong gains."   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  came after the kiwi surged to its strongest level in 22 years against the greenback last Thursday following the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's unexpected move to raise its interest rate by a quarter-point to a record 8% -- the highest among major economies.   \par \par \uc2 The rising global interest in carry trades -- in which investors borrow low-yielding \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , such as the yen, and reinvest in higher-yielding \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  -- has boosted demand for the New Zealand dollar in recent years.   \par \par \uc2 The New Zealand dollar has appreciated about 20% against the dollar and 30% against the yen in the past 12 months.   \par \par \uc2 A fight on its hands   \par \par \uc2 The rise in the value of the New Zealand dollar has led to worries that \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strength would hurt economic growth by making exports more expensive. Earlier this year, Bollard indicated that the level of the kiwi dollar was unjustified based on fundamentals.   \par \par \uc2 "If today's action by the [\b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ] is a statement of intent, then the bank may well have a fight on its hands," said Simon Derrick, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at  \uc2 The Bank of New York.\uc2  "Whilst wanting to offer some protection for the export sector, Bollard has made clear that he wishes to maintain a tight monetary policy."   \par \par \uc2 Masafumi Yamamoto, analyst at  \uc2 Citigroup\uc2 , said if the kiwi dollar does not stop appreciating, "it might be natural to assume that the bank may \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  again."   \par \par \uc2 But Kathy Lien, chief strategist at DailyFX.com, said while further \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is not out of the question, any further move "could be limited by the fact that New Zealand does not have much money to spend."   \par \par \uc2 The special fund that they have set up for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  only has approximately 7 billion \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollars or US$5.3 billion. "Their \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  war chest is small," she said.   \par \par \uc2 Sue Trinh, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at  \uc2 RBC Capital Markets\uc2 , said the surprise \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  could be a "distraction" from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's core policy objective, which is to fight inflation.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said after its June rate hike that "a sustained period of slower growth in domestic activity will be required" to alleviate inflation pressures. "This further increase in the [official cash rate] is to ensure that inflation outcomes remain consistent with achieving the target of 1 to 3% inflation on average over the medium term."   \par \par \uc2 Still, "without historical precedent, it will be difficult to judge how long [it] will be in the market to weaken the New Zealand dollar, and how much weaker \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  could go."   \par \par \uc2 Follow suit   \par \par \uc2 The unusual policy action by New Zealand's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has greater implications for risk appetite and carry trades, analysts say. It also sparked speculation whether other central banks may follow suit.   \par \par \uc2 For instance, the Bank of Japan has come under intense political pressure from its trade partners for the low level of the yen. Should Japanese officials follow suit and \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , investors' tolerate of risk may be upset and the market may see a sharp unwinding of carry trades, analysts say.   \par \par \uc2 Bank of New York\uc2 's Derrick said \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  could help shift the Group of Seven leading countries' stance on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The G7 nations, in the past, have been aiming at prompting \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  flexibility, as a way to pressure China to make its yuan more flexible.   \par \par \uc2 "How long will the governments and central banks of the "developed" world be prepared to continue with a policy of non-\b \highlight22\uc2 interventionism\b0 \highlight\uc2  when other nations continue to "manage" their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  seemingly to their own advantage and show little interest in changing these policies in the near future?" he said, in a note to clients. " As far as New Zealand is concerned the answer would appear to be: 'no longer.'"   \par \par \uc2 "This summer could mark a significant turning point for political thinking within G7 and beyond on the issue of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," he said.   \par \par \uc2 Remains attractive   \par \par \uc2 Despite Monday's decline, expectations for further rate hikes and a weak dollar will likely continue to support the New Zealand dollar, analysts said.   \par \par \uc2 "Ultimately Bollard is wrong. The New Zealand dollar is not at exceptional levels nor are they unjustified," Chandler said. "The market, which votes with its money, says the interest rate differential - 7.5% over Japan overnight rates, for example, trumps New Zealand's trade and current account deficits and the decline in the competitiveness of its manufacturing sector."   \par \par \uc2 "Unless the [Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2 ] plans on continuing to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , market forces will likely continue to favor the kiwi," he said, in a note. "Indeed the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  may be seen as offering a new buying opportunity."   \par \par \uc2 Citigroup\uc2 's Yamamoto said New Zealand's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  "remains attractive for mid-to long-term investors like many Japanese investors," as the levels of the interest rates in New Zealand are the highest among major countries and further tightening is expected.   \par \par \uc2 "However, those who aim for a short-term \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  gain should be discouraged by the RBNZ's move," he said.   \par \par \uc2 But Daragh Maher, strategist at French Bank Calyon, said he's "wary" of the outlook for the kiwi dollar.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's move "has introduced another downside risk that will have to be taken on board by those keen to buy the New Zealand dollar at such overvalued levels. "Policymakers have made it clear that they see limits to the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's upside."   \par \par \uc2 "The limits to the downside, by contrast, are some way distant." [ 06-11-07 1648ET ]   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJON000020070611e36b00015\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
