\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Economic Stories Of The Day   \b0\par\par\uc2 779 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Juni 2007\par 07:04\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par RBNZ CONFIRMS IT HAS \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENED\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  IN \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  MARKET, SOLD NZ DLR    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Reserve Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 New Zealand\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  confirmed it \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Monday in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market to sell the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 New Zealand\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dollar. (published 0400 GMT)   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =UPDATE: CHINA MAY PPI UP 2.8% ON YEAR VS UP 2.9% IN APRIL    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's producer price index rose 2.8% in May from a year earlier, a slower increase than the 2.9% gain in April, the National Bureau of Statistics said Monday. (published 0312 GMT)   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =UPDATE:HKMA YAM:1ST CNY BONDS LIKELY SMALL BUT RESPONSE GOOD    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Hong Kong \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Chief Executive Joseph Yam said he believes the market's response to yuan-denominated bonds in Hong Kong will be good given the rising value of the Chinese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and more favorable returns from bonds than savings. (published 0308 GMT)   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par JAPAN MOF:OMI,ITALIAN FIN MIN AGREE NEED MORE FLEXIBLE YUAN    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japanese Finance Minister Koji Omi and his Italian counterpart agreed that China should make its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  more flexible, a Japanese MOF official said Monday. (published 0211 GMT)   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par CHINA ECON PLANNER: JAN-MAY CHINA POWER GENERATION +15.8%    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's power generation rose 15.8% in the first five months of this year, its fastest pace of growth in three years, the country's economic planning agency said. (published 0051 GMT)   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =UPDATE: JAPAN JAN-MAR REVISED GDP +0.8% Q/Q; PRELIM +0.6%    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Japanese government Monday revised up the economic growth rate for the January-March period, saying business investment was stronger than initially estimated. (published 0004 GMT)   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par NZ MAY HOUSE PRICES RISE AT FASTEST ON-YEAR PACE IN 10 MOS-QV    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 New Zealand's annual housing inflation accelerated at its fastest pace in 10 months in May, a survey released late Sunday by government agency Quotable Value showed. (published 0008 GMT)   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par MALAYSIA PM: WORLD TO STAY DEPENDENT ON "WEST ASIA" OIL    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The world has sufficient oil and gas reserves despite concerns they are running out soon, and the key challenge is gaining access to them, Malaysia's prime minister said Monday. (published 0215 GMT)   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =DATA SNAP: NZ 1Q TERMS OF TRADE +2.0% VS 4Q; EXPECTED +2.5%    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 New Zealand's terms of trade, a gauge of the country's international purchasing power, rose in the first quarter as import prices decreased more than exports, official figures published Monday showed. (published 2302 GMT)   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par SENIOR IRANIAN ENVOY TO MEET WITH IAEA OFFICIAL - SOURCES    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 After years of stonewalling, Iran is sending a senior envoy to Vienna for talks that could provide answers on past nuclear activities to the U.N. nuclear monitoring agency investigating its atomic program, diplomats said. (published 0105 GMT)   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     ======= DOW JONES NEWSWIRES ANALYSIS AND COMMENTARY ======= \par  \par  \par WSJE(6/11) BREAKINGVIEWS: US FED OVERNIGHT RATE AT 8%?    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Investors are starting to worry that the U.S. Federal Reserve will have to push overnight interest rates up in order to get inflation under firm control. But how much higher than the current 5.25% will the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  have to go? If New Zealand is any guide, something like 8% might be called for. (published 0430 GMT)   \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  OPTIONS:DLR/YEN VOLATILITIES UP;MAY FALL NEXT FEW DAYS    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Volatilities implied by dollar/yen \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  options rose slightly in Tokyo Monday as players bought back options ahead of U.S. economic data due out later in the week. (published 0434 GMT)   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =DATA VIEW: JAPAN'S STRONG CAPEX PROMPTS GDP UPWARD REVISION    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan Monday revised up its reading on the economy's growth rate for the first three months of this year because business investment was much stronger than initially thought. (published 0325 GMT)   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =CHARTING \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 : DLR UP VS MOST MAJORS THIS WK;DN VS AUD, NZD    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 USD/JPY may consolidate this week. The daily indicators are mixed as the stochastic is bullish, but the MACD remains bearish. Immediate resistance is at 122.19, the Jan. 29 high. (published 0023 GMT)   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =HOT TOPIC: DATA THIS WEEK TO KEEP PBOC ON ITS TOES    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Authorities in China should get further impetus this week to maintain a tightening stance on the economy - but they are likely to hold off on taking fresh action. (published 2329 GMT)   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =US MONEY WEEK AHEAD: TREASURYS MAY NEED MORE THAN SURGERY    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 There was a surgical precision to the Treasurys market's latest repricing, which sent long-dated yields back to last year's peaks but left no scar on broader financial markets. (published 2200 GMT)   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =CHARTING MARKETS: EURO TO EDGE HIGHER AGAINST DOLLAR    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In case of an early rally, first resistance is a potential intraday high. (published 2200 GMT)   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 11-06-07 0504GMT ]   \f28 \par \par \uc2 1030 1804 4180   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020070611e36b0004o\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
