\par\par \b \uc2 RBNZ: Won't Comment On Market Rumors Of  \highlight22\uc2 FX Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 202 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Juni 2007\par 05:25\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 WELLINGTON (Dow Jones)--The Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  Monday declined to comment on talk that it is \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to pull back a strong local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 "Our stance is we don't comment on these things," an RBNZ spokesman said.   \par \par \uc2 Several traders in Tokyo and \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  said they have heard talk of the RBNZ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but none could confirm that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had sold the New Zealand \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 The New Zealand dollar, which tapped a fresh post-float peak of US$0.7640 Friday in New York, has fallen sharply over the past hour to US$0.7527 from US$0.7625.   \par \par \uc2 RBNZ Governor Alan Bollard had last week reiterated a previous statement that the New Zealand dollar is exceptionally high and unjustified by medium-term fundamentals, which traders say portended potential \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the bank.   \par \par \uc2 Bollard last week played down \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  talk, but acknowledged that the use of the words "exceptional" and "unjustified" meets two of four criteria needed for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market.   \par \par \uc2 -By Shri Navaratnam, Dow Jones Newswires; +64-4-471-5990; shri.navaratnam@dowjones.com [ 11-06-07 0341GMT ]   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020070611