\par\par \b \uc2 NZ dollar slips after cenbank warning   \b0\par\par\uc2 336 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 April 2007\par 07:36\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 WELLINGTON, April 27 (Reuters) - The New Zealand dollar slipped on Friday, after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's warning on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  the previous day sparked speculation among some traders of possible \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 But most analysts think the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  is unlikely to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  given the kiwi's current strength is partly due to weakness in the U.S. dollar and as a weaker \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  would have an inflationary impact on imported goods.   \par \par \uc2 "\b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets were a little spooked by the comment that the level of exchange rate was 'unjustified' relative to medium-term fundamentals," said Danica Hampton, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 "At this stage, we don't think \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is a real threat, and we view (Governor Alan) Bollard's comments on the NZD as simply a clever way of taking the sting out of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  following the rate hike."   \par \par \uc2 By 0510 GMT, the New Zealand dollar was trading around $0.74 <NZD=>, compared with $0.7480/82 in late local trade on Thursday and a 22-year post-float high of $0.7493 <NZD=D2> reached last week.   \par \par \uc2 The RBNZ raised interest rates to 7.75 percent on Thursday but did not mention whether a further tightening would be necessary as it did in previous statements.   \par \par \uc2 Many traders expect the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to remain vigilant over inflation pressures which will likely support the kiwi.   \par \par \uc2 "Until markets become convinced the RBNZ's actions are slowing growth, robust domestic demand is likely to keep the NZD/USD well supported on dips," Hampton said.   \par \par \uc2 Data showed on Friday electronic retail card spending fell for the first time in eight months in March, but analysts said it still pointed to solid consumer demand which will likely keep interest rates elevated into next year.   \par \par \uc2 Government bonds rebounded, with yields slipping around 2 basis points along the curve.   \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-NEWZEALAND-DOLLAR (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|ND|AUF|ABX|RBN|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070430e34r0009l\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
