\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-RBNZ's Bollard says  \highlight22\uc2 forex intervention \highlight\uc2  an option  \b0\par\par\uc2 388 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Dezember 2006\par 20:55\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (Adds market reaction, details)  \par \par \uc2 WELLINGTON, Dec 8 (Reuters) - The Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  could \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market if it considered the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to be "exceptionally and unjustifiably high", Governor Alan Bollard was quoted as saying on Friday.  \par \par \uc2 "If we think it's exceptionally and unjustifiably high and we think that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is an option for us, then we've got the tools to do that. So we'll always consider that," Bollard told TVOne. The New Zealand dollar <NZD=> dropped about a quarter of a cent to around $0.6870 following Bollard's comments, pulling back from a 10-\u189\'00\'BD month high of $0.6922 reached on Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 On Thursday, the RBNZ held interest rates at 7.25 percent -- the highest in the industrialised world -- but warned it may have to raise them again due to a stronger-than-expected domestic economy, sparking a rally in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and short-term yields.  \par \par \uc2 The Reserve Bank has always had the power to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, by directly selling the \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar, but has not done so since the New Zealand dollar was floated in 1985.  \par \par \uc2 In 2004, the RBNZ received a NZ$1 billion capital injection to bolster its reserves in case it needed to buy or sell the New Zealand dollar, prompting speculation the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was going to be more \b \highlight22\uc2 interventionist\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 The bank has said it will step in only if the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is at exceptional levels not justified by economic fundamentals, the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  can be expected to be successful, and it is consistent with the bank's role of achieving price stability.  \par \par \uc2 Speculation of a possible RBNZ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was rekindled last year after Bollard described the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  as being "exceptionally high".  \par \par \uc2 In Thursday's monetary policy statement, Bollard warned that sustained strength in the New Zealand dollar could threaten the ongoing re-balancing of the economy.  \par \par \uc2 The strong kiwi dollar has been partly blamed for New Zealand's annual current account deficit swelling to a record high NZ$15.15 billion ($10.45 billion), or 9.7 percent of gross domestic product, as of the September quarter. ($1=NZ$1.45)  \par \par \uc2 NEWZEALAND-BOLLARD/ (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ND|ABN|D|E|RBN|M|AUF|ABX|RNP|DNP  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020061207e2c70030x\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
