\par\par \b \uc2 RPT-ANALYSIS-NZ cenbank's hands seen tied on  \highlight22\uc2 FX intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 By Kazunori Takada  \par \uc2 606 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 November 2005\par 19:24\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 WELLINGTON, Nov 14 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is caught in a conundrum: how to engineer an export-boosting fall in its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  when such a fall would likely stoke inflation and force a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -boosting rise in interest rates.  \par \par \uc2 Faced with a record current account deficit, Reserve Bank of New Zealand Governor Alan Bollard has railed against what he sees as an unjustifiably high Kiwi dollar.  \par \par \uc2 But with almost the same breath he warns that a drop in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  would further aggravate inflation and could lead to a rise in interest rates -- already the highest in the industrialised world at 7.0 percent.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could always \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  directly to sell \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollars. Recently Bollard referred to the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  as being "exceptionally high," a term used by the RBNZ to describe one of its conditions for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar <NZD=> has eased from a 23-year high against the U.S. dollar, but on a trade-weighted basis <=NZD>, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's preferred measure, it remains near record peaks.  \par \par \uc2 "All this sounds like a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  which has the mindset where it will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Greg Gibbs, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at RBC Capital Markets.  \par \par \uc2 Gibbs said a rise in the trade-weighted index (TWI) to new highs and the New Zealand dollar's climb above its recent peak against the Australian dollar <AUDNZD=R>, the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  of its biggest trading parter, could prompt the Reserve Bank to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 The high exchange rate has ravaged the country's export sector. The annual current account deficit hit 8 percent of gross domestic product in the second quarter and is still widening.  \par \par \uc2 CONDITIONS NOT MET  \par \par \uc2 The Reserve Bank has always had the power to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, but has not done so since the New Zealand dollar was floated in 1985.  \par \par \uc2 Last year, the RBNZ received a NZ$1 billion capital injection to bolster reserves in the event it needed to buy and sell the New Zealand dollar, prompting analysts to think the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was going to be more \b \highlight22\uc2 interventionist\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 But many analysts think the chances Bollard will act on his warnings are slim because the conditions spelt out by the RBNZ for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  have not all been met and, given current circumstances, are actually contradictory.  \par \par \uc2 The bank has said it will step in only if the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is at exceptional levels not justified by economic fundamentals; the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  can be expected to be successful and is consistent with the bank's role of achieving price stability.  \par \par \uc2 The first condition is considered fulfilled given the relative high exchange rate and a slowing economy.  \par \par \uc2 But analysts doubt \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would depress the kiwi dollar for long given foreign appetite for the kiwi's high yield has seen a record NZ$21 billion ($14.4 billion) of eurobond issuance this year.  \par \par \uc2 More fundamentally, weakening the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  would also put upward pressure on imported inflation and thus work against the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's tight monetary policy.  \par \par \uc2 Annual inflation rose to a five-year high of 3.4 percent in the third quarter, breaking above the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's target band of 1.0 to 3.0 percent. And strong wage and employment data out last week, point to further pressure ahead.  \par \par \uc2 "They would probably take the view that if we are still in a situation to raise interest rates, we shouldn't be trying to weaken the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Darren Gibbs, senior economist at Deutsche Bank.  \par \par \uc2 (US$1=NZ$1.4552)  \par \par \uc2 x|LANGEN|ND  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020051114e1be0021j\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
