\par\par \b \uc2 RBNZ: Any  \highlight22\uc2 FX Intervention \highlight\uc2  Likely To Be Aggressive, Public  \b0\par\par\uc2 674 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 April 2005\par 04:26\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 WELLINGTON (Dow Jones)--\b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  says that if exercises its recently granted \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  power in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market it will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  aggressively and quickly make public its actions.  \par \par \uc2 In an article published in the latest Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  Bulletin late last week, the bank reiterates its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy and reveals how it would carry out any \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market dealings.  \par \par \uc2 "The style of execution will be relatively aggressive. The Bank will ask market participants to quote it a price and would deal on those prices, thereby forcing transactions into the market," the Reserve Bank said.  \par \par \uc2 "This approach is more likely to result in the bank's counterparts quickly acting to pass on the bank's deals to others, creating ongoing transaction activity in the direction the bank desires, maximizing the impact on the exchange rate."  \par \par \uc2 The Reserve Bank states that "often, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  will be very open and public."  \par \par \uc2 "In these cases, the Bank will issue a press release shortly after having \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 , noting it has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the rationale for the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ."  \par \par \uc2 The bank said it will comment on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  "if it thinks such commentary is useful in enhancing the effectiveness of the \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2 ."  \par \par \uc2 "Sometimes, though, the Bank may wish to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  covertly, which will mean that there will be no comment from the Bank at the time of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ."  \par \par \uc2 Last year the Reserve Bank was given the means to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar market when the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is "exceptionally" high or low, relative to the level that economic fundamentals suggest it should be at. Before that mandate, the Reserve Bank was allowed to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  only during a financial crisis.  \par \par \uc2 Despite the Kiwi, as the New Zealand dollar is known, rising to a 22-year high of US$0.7465 last month, the Reserve Bank doesn't yet appear to have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market  \par \par \uc2 In the article by Kelly Eckhold of the Reserve Bank's Financial Stability Department and Chris Hunt of the bank's Economics Department, the Reserve Bank reiterates its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy of not trying to fight market trends.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    RBNZ Would Probably \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  In NZD/USD \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Instead, the Reserve Bank will wait until market participants become less sure about the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's direction, the balance of capital flows shifts toward pushing the exchange rate back toward equilibrium and there is a relative absence of capital flows that might offset \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Reserve Bank also revealed how it is likely to carry out any actual \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 It will usually \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 New Zealand\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dollar/US dollar \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  pair, because it is the most liquid and because most other \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  pairs are derived with reference to that exchange rate.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Transaction actions will generally be with wholesale market participants and would typically be of a similar size as the standard market parcel of NZ$10 million or more.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "To maximize the strength of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  signal the Bank is likely to transact with a number of market makers simultaneously," the Reserve Bank said.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Usually, when the Reserve Bank transacts in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market, it tries to minimize the impact.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The execution approach in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  situations will be quite the opposite, as the aim of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operation\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  would be to maximize the exchange rate impact," the Reserve Bank said.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "This implies that the Bank would look to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at times when there is relatively little interest by other market participants to trade against it."  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Reserve Bank said it will use the opposite approach when unwinding any \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  positions gained as a result of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The associated transactions will be performed in a manner consistent with minimizing the impact on the exchange rate," the bank said.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "For example, the Bank will pick times when there are a number of other investors interested in trading in the opposite direction, and its execution style will be very passive."  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 - By Christopher Niesche, Dow Jones Newswires; 64-4-471-5990; christopher.niesche@dowjones.com [ 04-04-05 0226GMT ]  \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020050404e1440001t\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
