\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2-NZ sounds alarm bells over  \highlight22\uc2 currency \highlight\uc2  strength.  \b0\par\par\uc2 699 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2005\par 08:26\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 MELBOURNE, March 9 (Reuters) - New Zealand sounded alarm bells on Wednesday over the rise in the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to 22-year highs above 74 U.S. cents, concerned it could damage the country's trade position.  \par \par \uc2 The New Zealand dollar, known as the kiwi in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, rose to a high of 74.06 U.S. cents ahead of a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  meeting on Thursday to review interest rates.  \par \par \uc2 "Let's see whether that's temporary or not, whether it's a blip in advance of a Reserve Bank announcement, which you sometimes see," Finance Minister Michael Cullen told Reuters.  \par \par \uc2 "Clearly, at that level, it does start to become a very real concern," he said, after speaking at a financial conference in Melbourne.  \par \par \uc2 The kiwi fell after Cullen's comments to a low of 73.58 U.S. cents before recovering to last trade at 73.69/79 U.S. cents.  \par \par \uc2 A near 90 percent rise in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  since October 2000 has cut into the earnings of exporters, such as forestry company Carter Holt Harvey, and was cited this week for putting two sawmills and a wood processing plant out of business.  \par \par \uc2 Exports generate the equivalent of one third of gross domestic product. The country's primary products, such as dairy and meat, account for about 40 percent of annual exports worth NZ$31 billion ($23 billion).  \par \par \uc2 Record commodity prices have helped insulate farmers from the brunt of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's strength, which makes imports cheaper.  \par \par \uc2 "But it tends to keep driving the current account deficit, which is getting uncomfortably high," Cullen said.  \par \par \uc2 New Zealand accumulated a trade deficit of NZ$3.9 billion ($2.9 billion) in the year through January, just below the record NZ$4.2 billion in the year through December.  \par \par \uc2 The current account deficit ballooned to 5.8 percent of gross domestic product in the third quarter from a low of 2.5 percent at the end of 2001.  \par \par \uc2 HIGH, BUT FOR HOW LONG?  \par \par \uc2 Bob Walters, the chief executive of Export New Zealand, which represents around 4,000 exporters, said the New Zealand dollar's strength could soon become more of a problem for its members.  \par \par \uc2 "I guess the real concern of most of our members is how long is it going to continue at these relatively high levels - I would think a lot of them are getting very close to the end of hedging," he said.  \par \par \uc2 Dairy exporter Fonterra Co-operative Group Ltd., New Zealand's largest company, has said the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's lofty heights will depress payouts to its 13,000 farmer suppliers in the 2005/06 season, when commodity prices are expected to ease from record levels.  \par \par \uc2 World prices for 13 New Zealand commodities measured by ANZ Bank rose to a record high in February. The value of the products in local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  terms fell 0.3 percent from a month earlier, but were still 9.3 percent higher than a year earlier.  \par \par \uc2 Cullen said there was little the government could do about the dollar's level, but the Reserve Bank had certain limited resources it could use where it saw a risk to systemic stability.  \par \par \uc2 "If the level of the dollar creates some sort of systemic problem within the economy or within the financial system the bank now has the capacity to engage in limited action," he said.  \par \par \uc2 "The bank makes that determination and I don't comment on that at all."  \par \par \uc2 Last year, the government expanded the powers of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.  \par \par \uc2 Most analysts expect the \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar to fall in value later in the year as economic growth slows.  \par \par \uc2 But a run of stronger-than-expected data has raised the risk that New Zealand might raise interest rates, already the highest in the industrialised world, again on Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 A Reuters poll narrowly expected the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to leave the official cash rate at 6.5 percent, estimating the risk of a rate hike at 45 percent.  \par \par \uc2 Reserve Bank of New Zealand governor Alan Bollard will issue a monetary policy statement on Thursday at 9 a.m. (2000 GMT Wednesday).   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050309e13900015\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
