\par\par \b \uc2 NZ Fin Min: Not Entirely Comfortable With NZD Levels  \b0\par\par\uc2 284 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Oktober 2004\par 22:57\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 WELLINGTON (Dow Jones)--New Zealand Finance Minister Michael Cullen Wednesday said he is "not entirely" comfortable with the high level of the \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar but stopped short of advocating \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Reserve Bank.  \par \par \uc2 "I am not entirely comfortable with the position at the present time but luckily we have high commodity prices and it is muting the high oil prices," Cullen said.  \par \par \uc2 Cullen, who was speaking at the parliament's Finance and Expenditure Select Committee, said that confidence among exporters also is "surprisingly high" despite the high local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 When asked if the Reserve Bank should \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to bring down the \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar, Cullen said that is a decision for the bank. [ 19-10-04 2125GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 The New Zealand dollar has risen sharply by over 30% since the start of 2003, and has so far gained 5% this year to early Wednesday's levels of US$0.6860.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rose to a seven-year high of US$0.7102 in February - which had capped an 82% gain from its post-1985 float low of US$0.3898 hit in October 2000.  \par \par \uc2 Earlier this year, the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  was granted the capacity to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  when the local dollar reached "exceptional and unjustifiable" levels by Parliament.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has given little away on its plans, but \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market participants think there is a chance the RBNZ could test its new powers the next time the Kiwi - as the local dollar is popularly known - climbs near the US$0.7000 level.  \par \par \uc2 -By Christopher Niesche, Dow Jones Newswires; 64-4-471-5990; christopher.niesche@dowjones.com [ 19-10-04 2131GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020041019e0aj000xo\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
