\par\par \b \uc2 INTERVIEW: NZD  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Policy May Have Short Life  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Stephen Wright  \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES  \par \uc2 732 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2004\par 03:30\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 WELLINGTON (Dow Jones)--\b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2 's main opposition party, the center-right National, will deny the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  the multiparty support it wants for a new \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy, and will consider removing the bank's power to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  independently when it next becomes the government.  \par \par \uc2 National's associate finance spokesman, John Key, a former head of global \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  for investment bank Merrill Lynch, said Wednesday the party would vote against a motion in Parliament to approve changes to the funding agreement between the government and the Reserve Bank of New Zealand.  \par \par \uc2 Those changes will pave the way for \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves held for national emergencies - such as an outbreak of foot and mouth disease destroying confidence in the country's financial markets and making it impossible to trade the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  - to be increased by NZ$1.9 billion to NZ$7 billion over four years.  \par \par \uc2 More controversially, the amendments will allow the Reserve Bank to use an undisclosed amount of funds for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to trim the peaks and troughs of the exchange rate cycle, and will inject NZ$1 billion into the bank so its balance sheet can absorb marked-to-market losses on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  positions.  \par \par \uc2 Key said National supports emergency reserves being increased because the economy has grown significantly since the target level for reserves was last changed in 1998, but the party opposes New Zealand breaking with the clean float of its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  hasn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market since the local dollar was floated in March 1985.  \par \par \uc2 "We are not going to support" the change to the funding agreement when it is voted on in Parliament, Key told Dow Jones Newswires in an interview. The date for the Parliament vote hasn't been announced.  \par \par \uc2 The Reserve Bank earlier this month appealed for multiparty support for the policy change, saying this would reduce the risk of a "policy u-turn" that could result in marked-to-market losses becoming real losses.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par               Policy Change Certain To Pass \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Despite the National Party's opposition, ratification by Parliament is assured because the left-wing Green Party has said it would vote with the minority Labour-led coalition, giving it a majority.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The next National government would consider taking away the Reserve Bank's right to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market independently of the government if the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  hasn't \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the time National is elected government, Key said.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 When the policy change is passed, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  would still need government approval to use its emergency reserves, but \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to influence the level of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 New Zealand\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dollar would be conducted independently of the government.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 National currently has a large lead over the Labour-led government in opinion polls, but the next election doesn't have to be held until late 2005.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Key said if the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and still had open \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  positions by the time National forms the government, the party won't force it to close those positions "because they could be under water" and to buy those positions back could produce "very significant" losses for the New Zealand taxpayer.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "We are not going to cut off our nose to spite our face...If they haven't \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at the time we come into office, then I guess we will take a fresh look at that (\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  policy) and will determine whether we want to take away from them the right" to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , he said.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 National opposes \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 New Zealand\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dollar market because the "likely returns are small and the risks are quite great," Key said.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "We don't think it will actually do very much at all in terms of the exchange rate movement. The reality is that they will only get involved at the tops or bottoms of the cycle, which as the Treasury Department highlighted, is very difficult to do.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "And it creates a huge amount of moral hazard. I think what will happen - inevitably, businesses will become more reliant on a belief that the government can actually change the exchange rate when the proven evidence is they can't," he said.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Stephen Wright, Dow Jones Newswires; 64-4-471-5990; stephen.wright@dowjones.com  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -Edited by Dawn Lye [ 31-03-04 0130GMT ]  \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020040331e03v0001e\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
