\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-RBNZ to get NZ$2.9 bln for  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 -FinMin.  \b0\par\par\uc2 498 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2004\par 03:55\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2  WELLINGTON, March 30 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is to get a NZ$1 billion ($650 million) capital injection as part of its plan to cope with the high flying \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , while the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves will be increased by another NZ$1.9 billion, Finance Minister Michael Cullen said on Tuesday.   \par \par \uc2  Earlier this month the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  (RBNZ) asked the government for the capacity to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets at times when the \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar reached extreme and unjustifiable levels.   \par \par \uc2  The cash injection would allow the RBNZ to cover any losses incurred during \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Cullen said.   \par \par \uc2  The increased \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves are earmarked for use only at times of crisis when markets are "dysfunctional".   \par \par \uc2  "These measures should assist the economy by tempering exchange rate volatility," Cullen said in a statement.   \par \par \uc2  In a letter to Cullen from the RBNZ, released at the same time, the bank repeated its approach to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2  This included entering markets only at times when the kiwi was at extreme levels not justified by economic fundamentals; \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  when there is a real chance of influencing the market; not targeting any particular level of the dollar and, not going against the long term trend of the exchange rate.   \par \par \uc2  The New Zealand dollar was unmoved, sitting within its opening narrow range around $0.6510.   \par \par \uc2  Deutsche Bank chief economist Ulf Schoefisch said the latest release added little to what was already known.   \par \par \uc2  "We believe that the ongoing implications for \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets will be relatively minor," he said.   \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has said several times since it unveiled its proposals that any \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would be opportunistic and look only to trim the highs and lows of the exchange cycle.   \par \par \uc2  The New Zealand dollar , known as the kiwi, has risen about 19 percent against the U.S. dollar over the past year, largely driven by the greenback's slide and New Zealand's 425 basis point interest rate advantage.   \par \par \uc2  The RBNZ's overall foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  position would be limited, governor Alan Bollard said in the letter.   \par \par \uc2  Over the medium term the bank would aim to maintain, on average, a net zero open \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  position, and it would get out of the market when the exchange rate was not at "exceptional levels" and when they could "avoid influencing the exchange rate".   \par \par \uc2  New Zealand's overall \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves currently stand at NZ$5.1 billion, including Debt Management Office holdings and International Monetary Fund special drawing rights.   \par \par \uc2  The RBNZ's capital would be increased through raising its investment in government bonds.   \par \par \uc2  The planned NZ$1.9 billion increase in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  assets would be done over a four year period to lessen any impact on markets.   \par \par \uc2  Cullen said a motion needed to ratify a change to the RBNZ's funding agreement has been introduced into the 120 seat parliament, where it has majority support.   \par \par \uc2  ($1=NZ$1.54).   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040330e03u00061\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
