\par\par \b \uc2 NZ To Borrow To Increase  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank Forex \highlight\uc2  Reserves  \b0\par\par\uc2 338 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2004\par 01:39\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 WELLINGTON (Dow Jones)--The New Zealand government will increase its gross debt over the next four years to fund a significant increase in the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves, making it more difficult for the government to beat its target of gross debt averaging 30% of the economy, according to a Cabinet paper released Tuesday.  \par \par \uc2 Release of the document follows Finance Minister Michael Cullen's announcement Tuesday that the Reserve Bank of New Zealand's emergency \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves will be increased by NZ$1.9 billion to NZ$7 billion and the bank will also be given reserves, of an undisclosed amount, for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to temper peaks and troughs in the \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar's exchange rate cycle.  \par \par \uc2 "The increase in foreign reserves for market stabilization purposes is likely to occur in phases over the four years, although it could be brought forward if the need arises," Cullen said in the Cabinet paper.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will also need to build reserves for the new policy of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to influence the level of the \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar, he said.  \par \par \uc2 "The increase in reserves will add to gross sovereign debt, although the precise impact depends on when the bank calls on the resources, and the detail of the transaction between the New Zealand Debt Management Office and the bank," the paper said.  \par \par \uc2 The increase in gross debt would "reduce the extent to which the government is likely to overachieve" on its long-term debt objective of gross debt equaling 30% of gross domestic product on average.  \par \par \uc2 New Zealand's net debt would be "largely unchanged" as the borrowed funds will be invested in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  assets, Cullen said.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is also to get an injection of NZ$1 billion of new equity to help its balance sheet cope with the financial risks of the new \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy.  \par \par \uc2 -By Stephen Wright, Dow Jones Newswires; 64-4-471-5990; stephen.wright@dowjones.com [ 29-03-04 2339GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020040329e03t00131\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
