\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE: NZ  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2 's  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Reserves To Be Boosted  \b0\par\par\uc2 593 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2004\par 01:05\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 (Updates throughout with detail, background)  \par \par \uc2 WELLINGTON (Dow Jones)--New Zealand Finance Minister Michael Cullen said Tuesday the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves for stabilizing the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market during periods of dysfunction will be raised by NZ$1.9 billion to NZ$7 billion and further undisclosed funds will be approved for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to trim the peaks and troughs of the exchange rate cycle.  \par \par \uc2 The Reserve Bank of New Zealand also released a raft of papers and correspondence between itself and the finance minister about \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but all references to the amount of money the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will have for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to trim the extremes of exchange rate cycle - the key information for markets - was removed from the documents.  \par \par \uc2 The papers indicate it could take up to four years for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's emergency reserves to be increased to NZ$7 billion, or 2.45 billion Special Drawing Rights, a notional \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  used by the International Monetary Fund.  \par \par \uc2 The necessary changes to the Reserve Bank of New Zealand's funding agreement with the government will be voted on in parliament Tuesday. The legislature is expected to ratify the change in policy as the left-wing Green Party has said it will vote with the minority Labour-led government on the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  issue.  \par \par \uc2 The finance minister also said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's equity will be increased by about NZ$1 billion to help it cope with the financial risks associated with the new policy of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar market.  \par \par \uc2 Earlier this month the Reserve Bank asked the government for greater capacity to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to temper the \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar's rise.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  holds reserves to keep the New Zealand dollar market functioning in periods of market dysfunction but hasn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  since the local dollar was floated in 1985.  \par \par \uc2 Last month the New Zealand dollar hit a seven-year high of US$0.7102 against the U.S. dollar, which was a gain of 82% since its post 1985-float low of US$0.3898 which it hit in October 2000.  \par \par \uc2 The new aspect of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy gives the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  the capacity to buy or sell the New Zealand dollar when it is either exceptionally low or high relative to the level that economic fundamentals suggest it should be at.  \par \par \uc2 This type of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  will be carried out independently by the Reserve Bank using powers it has under Section 16 of the Reserve Bank Act.  \par \par \uc2 "These measures should assist the economy by tempering exchange rate volatility and will move New Zealand monetary management closer toward Australian practice," Cullen said.  \par \par \uc2 "They are strongly supported by the government as they are consistent with the changes we have introduced to monetary policy since taking office in 1999."  \par \par \uc2 In other changes, Cullen has given the Reserve Bank the power to use its emergency reserves without seeking the finance minister's permission.  \par \par \uc2 "In a period of market dysfunction, it is recognized that the bank may need to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  very quickly," Cullen said in a memorandum to the bank dated March 25.  \par \par \uc2 Cullen has given the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  a standing direction under Section 17 of the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  Act to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  using funds of up to 175 million SDRs when \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is urgently required but the finance minister or his deputies can't be contacted quickly.  \par \par \uc2 -By Stephen Wright, Dow Jones Newswires; 64-4-471-5990; stephen.wright@dowjones.com [ 29-03-04 2305GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020040329e03t0012p\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
