\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-RBNZ argues for NZD  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 , ready to act.  \b0\par\par\uc2 397 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2004\par 07:39\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 WELLINGTON, March 25 (Reuters) - The Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  repeated on Thursday that it was ready to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, saying it could be modestly effective as long as the timing was right.  \par \par \uc2 Since the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said two weeks ago it would seek authority to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , markets have been sceptical that the RBNZ could make much of a difference because its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves standa at a modest NZ$3.5 billion ($2.3 billion).  \par \par \uc2 The New Zealand dollar, known as the kiwi, has surged about 19 percent against the U.S. dollar over the past year. The rise has been driven largely by the greenback's slide, as well as New Zealand's 425 basis point interest rate advantage.  \par \par \uc2 RBNZ Deputy governor Adrian Orr said that while \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  could not reverse bigger international trends, it could still could be effective.  \par \par \uc2 "The Bank would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  at opportune times, not when the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's direction is being dominated by strong international trends or consensus opinions," Orr said in a speech prepared for delivery to a meat industry conference.  \par \par \uc2 At best \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would likely only soften the extreme tops and bottoms of a cycle, he said.  \par \par \uc2 Over the past three-and-a-half years the kiwi has touched a low of just below $0.39 in late 2000 and a high around $0.7100 in February.  \par \par \uc2 INCREASE RESERVES  \par \par \uc2 The RBNZ asked the government for the capacity to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets when the \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar moved to extreme and unjustifiable levels out of touch with economic fundamentals.  \par \par \uc2 Orr said the RBNZ wanted to increase significantly its current \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves, which have stayed at about the same level since the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was floated in 1985, and are earmarked for use in times of crisis when markets become "disorderly".  \par \par \uc2 The bank has also asked for a capital injection so it can absorb any temporary losses it might incur in any \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 The plan to buy and sell \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollars made "good portfolio management sense" over the long term, Orr said.  \par \par \uc2 "On average over the medium term we anticipate having no exposure to \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  swings."  \par \par \uc2 Orr said the proposed system should not attract speculators to "take the Bank on", and the RBNZ believed the risks were relatively small and manageable. ($1=NZ$1.54).   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040325e03p001cz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
