\par\par \b \uc2 NZ dollar trundles after euro, trades tight range.  \b0\par\par\uc2 431 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2004\par 23:34\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 AUCKLAND, March 24 (Reuters) - The New Zealand dollar was trundling around in the wake of the euro on Wednesday, trading in a tight range after failing to push convincingly higher overnight.  \par \par \uc2 The kiwi dollar was however enjoying some "safe haven" support, while the markets awaited more fallout from news that Israel had killed the spiritual leader of the militant group, Hamas.  \par \par \uc2 The kiwi had spent most of the night tracking the euro but had traded a relatively narrow $0.6589-25 range.  \par \par \uc2 By 10:10 a.m. (2210 GMT) it was at $0.6603/13 against $0.6599/06 in late trade on Tuesday.  \par \par \uc2 ANZ Investment Bank's director of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  John Body said the euro had tried to push back above 1.2350 but had failed.  \par \par \uc2 Likewise the New Zealand dollar had tried to run over the low $0.6600s when it met with heavy selling at around $0.6615.  \par \par \uc2 "That really put a wall on the topside and now it's just a matter of wait and see on what is going to develop in the political space in the Middle East over the next 24 hours and the impact that will have on the U.S. dollar," Body said.  \par \par \uc2 Markets were looking for safe havens and, for the moment, they appeared to be in the form of New Zealand, Australian and Canadian dollars , he said.  \par \par \uc2 Comments on \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  Finance Minister Michael Cullen had no influence on the market.  \par \par \uc2 The minister said in a speech that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets was a sensible way to try to discourage speculative excesses and herd behaviour that has driven the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 "It is difficult to be absolutely sure when this is the case; but where such behaviours can be identified it appears possible (and sensible) to try to change that behaviour," Cullen said in speech notes to a business forum.  \par \par \uc2 Cullen said the continued high level of the New Zealand dollar was worrying because it might discourage investment in the export sector and limit the country's ability to take advantage of the global upturn.  \par \par \uc2 New Zealand debt markets were little changed and were getting little direction from a muted U.S. Treasuries market as dealers awaited fourth quarter New Zealand balance of payments data on Thursday and gross domestic product data on Friday.  \par \par \uc2 February 2005 bonds were unchanged at 5.30 percent and November 2006s were at 5.31, down one.  \par \par \uc2 July 2009s were at 5.51 percent and April 2013s at 5.66, both unchanged.   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040323e03n003k8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
