\par\par \b \uc2 NZ Fin Min: Important To Ensure  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Policy Independent  \b0\par\par\uc2 457 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2004\par 21:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 WELLINGTON (Dow Jones)--New Zealand Finance Minister Michael Cullen said Wednesday he wants the nation's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to independently operate a proposed policy for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to dampen the local dollar's strength.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  poses financial risks and it is important that the revised \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy seeks to minimize those risks, the minister said in speech notes for a speech to a Deutsche Bank-organized investment conference in Auckland.  \par \par \uc2 "One important way this can be done is by ensuring the Reserve Bank Governor can operate this policy independently of day-to-day political pressures, that is, by keeping the focus on the medium term," said Cullen, who in the past few months has been trying to talk the New Zealand dollar down from its current high level.  \par \par \uc2 The government is considering proposals from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  for it to increase the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves it maintains for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to calm volatility in the local dollar - but hasn't used in 20 years - and to establish separate reserves for a new \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy aimed at smoothing out peaks and troughs in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Cullen said it is also important that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's foremost consideration remains meeting its Policy Targets Agreement objective of keeping annual consumer price inflation in a 1% to 3% band.  \par \par \uc2 "Indeed any revised policy on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is unlikely to alter the Policy Targets Agreement. It is merely another tool to help the Governor achieve those targets in the least cost manner.  \par \par \uc2 "It is consistent with the requirement in the Policy Targets Agreement for the (\b \highlight22\uc2 central) bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to seek to avoid unnecessary instability in the exchange rate," the finance minister said.  \par \par \uc2 Cullen reiterated that there "may be some merit" in having a greater capacity to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar market.  \par \par \uc2 This capacity would allow room for a policy that "aims to dampen the extreme peaks and troughs of an exchange rate cycle, that is, the three to five years swings from peak to trough in the exchange rate."  \par \par \uc2 The impact of any \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is unlikely to be large, Cullen said. "Maybe a few cents at the peaks and troughs of the cycle, or alternatively helping the cycle to turn a little earlier than otherwise would happen."  \par \par \uc2 The New Zealand dollar last month hit a seven year high of US$0.7102, which represented a gain of 82% from its post-1985 float low of US$0.3898 hit in October 2000.  \par \par \uc2 Keeping the New Zealand dollar a floating \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  will remain a key component of the nation's macroeconomic policy framework, Cullen said.  \par \par \uc2 -By Stephen Wright, Dow Jones Newswires; 64-4-471-5990; stephen.wright@dowjones.com [ 23-03-04 2000GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020040323e03n000xj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
