\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-RBNZ says no NZ dlr level in mind,  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  rare.   \b0\par\par\uc2 563 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2004\par 03:22\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  WELLINGTON, March 17 (Reuters) - The Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  will not target any particular level of exchange rate nor battle the market in the event it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, according to a background paper released on Wednesday.    \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  surprised last week when it said it would ask the government for the "capacity" to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market if the kiwi dollar  reached unjustifiable levels that were not in tune with economic fundamentals.    \par \par \uc2  The bank said in its background paper it would need a capital injection to give it the funds to be able to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 .    \par \par \uc2  Governor Alan Bollard later said any new funds should be kept separate from the current NZ$3.5 billion ($2.3 billion) \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves, which it wants kept in case of extreme cases when markets become "disorderly".    \par \par \uc2  Asked at a parliamentary committee how much extra money the bank would need, Bollard refused to give a figure.    \par \par \uc2  "We don't wish markets to take initial positions about what they think our ensuing positions might be," he said.    \par \par \uc2  The New Zealand dollar has gained around a quarter of a cent since the comments to last trade at $0.6533/40. That compared with Tuesday's late local level of around $0.6485.    \par \par \uc2  The kiwi dollar has gained around 19 percent against the greenback over the past year making it one of the best performers in the world, but also severely dented export earnings.    \par \par \uc2  RARE AND OPPORTUNISTIC    \par \par \uc2  Bank of New Zealand treasury economist Craig Ebert said neither the paper nor Bollard's appearance before the parliamentary committee added much to last week's announcement.    \par \par \uc2  "Broadly speaking (they were) fire fighting what seemed to be misunderstandings, they were really clarifying what they are not going to do," Ebert said.    \par \par \uc2  The RBNZ paper repeated previous comments that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would only occur when the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was at extreme levels not justified by economic fundamentals.    \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would be "rare" and "opportunistic", it said.    \par \par \uc2  "We do not expect to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  very often or to be able to alter the exchange rate by a sufficiently large amount to make this a substantial issue," it said.    \par \par \uc2  "The Bank will not be attempting to stop the exchange rate moving when economic adjustment would be helped by that movement - we will not be targeting or defending any particular exchange rate."    \par \par \uc2  The RBNZ already has the power to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  when financial markets are "disorderly" - when a price is not being offered in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  - but has never done so since the kiwi was floated in early 1985.    \par \par \uc2  Ebert said a large number of the "mechanics" of how the RBNZ would increase its reserves and operate in the market had yet to be worked through.    \par \par \uc2  "Even so I think the prospect of them \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  is quite low," Ebert said.    \par \par \uc2  Bollard said no work had been done on whether the bank might have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  at any time in the past.    \par \par \uc2  Over the past three-and-a-half years the kiwi has touched a low of just below $0.39 in late 2000 and a high last month around $0.7100.    \par \par \uc2  Any \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy could eventually be profitable for bank, the RBNZ said.    \par \par \uc2  "There is likely to be a small benefit from \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , enough to outweigh the comparatively small risks of implementing the policy."    \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040317e03h00070\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
