\par\par \b \uc2 NZ dollar claws back ground as RBNZ clarifies.  \b0\par\par\uc2 454 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2004\par 22:46\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     AUCKLAND, March 17 (Reuters) - The New Zealand dollar\par bounced back on Wednesday after the Reserve Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 New Zealand\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par clarified its position on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , saying it would only\par act in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market in extreme circumstances.\par     Dealers had last week's sharp sell-off, in part driven by\par the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's statement that it had proposed to seek the\par capacity to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , uppermost in their minds in the leadup\par to the release of Wednesday's background paper from the bank.\par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , which had already pushed through $0.6500,\par fell back in the minutes before the statement as the market\par re-positioned for the worst.\par  \par     "The market had memories of what happened last week," said\par one dealer.\par     But when the Reserve Bank said it would not target any\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 particular level of exchange rate nor battle the market in the  \f28 \par \par \uc2 event it ever \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, the  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was boosted over $0.6500.  \par \par \uc2 By 10:30 a.m. (2130 GMT) the kiwi was at $0.6503/10, up  \par \par \uc2 from $0.6481/91 at Wednesday's close, after trading in a  \par \par \uc2 $0.6477-$0.6527 range overnight.  \par \par \uc2 The RBNZ said in its paper any \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would occur  \par \par \uc2 only at the extremes of a exchange rate cycle and would be  \par \par \uc2 "opportunistic" and that it expected \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  to be  \par \par \uc2 infrequent.  \par \par \uc2 "We do not expect to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  very often or to be able to  \par \par \uc2 alter the exchange rate by a sufficiently large amount to make  \par \par \uc2 this a substantial issue," the paper said.  \par \par \uc2 "The Bank will not be attempting to stop the exchange rate  \par \par \uc2 moving when economic adjustment would be helped by that  \par \par \uc2 movement - we will not be targeting or defending any  \par \par \uc2 particular exchange rate," it said.  \par \par \uc2 More information was expected to emerge from Reserve Bank  \par \par \uc2 Governor Alan Bollard's appearance before the parliamentary  \par \par \uc2 finance and expenditure committee meeting later on Wednesday  \par \par \uc2 morning.  \par \par \uc2 Consolidation around $0.6500 appeared the order of the day.  \par \par \uc2 "With the New Zealand dollar better balanced now from a  \par \par \uc2 positioning perspective, both against the U.S. dollar and on  \par \par \uc2 the crosses, we favour a mild consolidation, with the key  \par \par \uc2 support level to the downside at $0.6370 favoured to hold,"  \par \par \uc2 Bank of New Zealand \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist Sue Trinh said in a  \par \par \uc2 commentary.  \par \par \uc2 New Zealand government bonds rallied in line with U.S.  \par \par \uc2 Treasuries after the U.S Federal Reserve sounded a note of  \par \par \uc2 caution about the labour market.  \par \par \uc2 Among the movements, February 2005 bonds were at 5.28  \par \par \uc2 percent from 5.32 at Tuesday's close, November 2006s at 5.30  \par \par \uc2 percent from 5.35, July 2009s at 5.46 percent from 5.53 and  \par \par \uc2 April 2013s at 5.61 percent from 5.69.  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040316e03g0030v\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
