\par\par \b \uc2 NZ Fin Min:  \highlight22\uc2 FX Intervention \highlight\uc2  Will Reduce NZD's Volatility  \b0\par\par\uc2 421 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2004\par 04:45\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 WELLINGTON (Dow Jones)--\b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market will "somewhat" reduce the local dollar's volatility and signal to markets that they can't bank on the government being "entirely supine" in its response to \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  speculation, Finance Minister Michael Cullen said Saturday.  \par \par \uc2 In notes for a speech to a regional conference of the governing Labour Party, Cullen reiterated he will soon take a recommendation to Cabinet that will "further align" New Zealand's monetary policy with close neighbor Australia's, including the ability to take a more active role in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  management.  \par \par \uc2 The Reserve Bank stunned local markets Thursday by announcing it had asked Cullen for the power to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  when the \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar is either "unjustifiably" high or low, sparking a 3% slide in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  over 24 hours.  \par \par \uc2 Cullen said \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  "will not remove the volatility" of the \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar "but it will reduce it somewhat, and, as importantly, signal to the financial sector that they cannot bank on us being entirely supine in response to their speculative behavior."  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  already has the power to sell or buy the New Zealand dollar when market conditions are dangerously volatile, but has never used that power since the local dollar was floated in March 1985.  \par \par \uc2 The change in policy requires parliament to ratify an amendment to the Reserve Bank's funding agreement, which will allow it to increase its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves.  \par \par \uc2 The minority Labour-led coalition government is assured of a majority for the vote because the left-wing Green Party has agreed to give its support.  \par \par \uc2 The New Zealand dollar last month reached a seven-year high of US$0.7102, which was a gain of 82% from October 2000 when it hit a post-float low of US$0.3898.  \par \par \uc2 Saturday the New Zealand dollar has been trading around US$0.6450 compared with US$0.6685 before the Reserve Bank's announcement Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 Cullen said the main reason for the New Zealand dollar's appreciation has been the "dramatic fall" in the U.S. dollar.  \par \par \uc2 "That has been caused by the combination in the U.S.A. of a large current account deficit and a burgeoning budget deficit, each many times the size of New Zealand's entire gross domestic product," he said.  \par \par \uc2 -By Stephen Wright, Dow Jones Newswires; 64-4-471-5990; stephen.wright@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 APDJ-03-12-04 2055GMT< [ 13-03-04 0345GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020040313e03d0000r\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
