\par\par \b \uc2 2nd UPDATE: NZ Confirms Break With  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  Nonintervention  \b0\par\par\uc2 860 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2004\par 03:02\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 (Updates with details of Green Party's support for the policy change, reaction from the major opposition National party.)  \par \par \uc2 WELLINGTON (Dow Jones)--New Zealand Finance Minister Michael Cullen and the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  have confirmed New Zealand will break with its near 20-year policy of not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets.  \par \par \uc2 The Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  earlier Thursday said it has asked Cullen to be allowed to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to influence the \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar when it is "unjustifiably" low or high.  \par \par \uc2 Cullen said he is "strongly supportive" of the bank's proposal. A Cabinet paper incorporating the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's advise is being drafted and will be presented to the Cabinet of government ministers in the near future.  \par \par \uc2 The finance minister has been hinting since late last year that \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2 's laissez faire policy of not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market since the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was floated in March 1985 would be abandoned.  \par \par \uc2 The change in policy will require approval from Cabinet and parliament. That is guaranteed after the left-wing Green Party, which has nine lawmakers in New Zealand's 120-member parliament, said it would vote with the minority Labour government, which has 52 seats in parliament.  \par \par \uc2 Last month, Cullen made his most specific comments on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , telling Dow Jones Newswires that he was awaiting advice from the Treasury Department and Reserve Bank, and warning traders not to count on the policy remaining the same.  \par \par \uc2 The New Zealand dollar has gained more than 70% against the U.S. dollar since hitting a post-float low of US$0.3898 in October 2000. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  gained 25% in each of 2002 and 2003, and earlier this year hit a seven-year high of US$0.7102.  \par \par \uc2 The strength of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is expected to cause a slowdown in the New Zealand economy over the next year due to lower export incomes.  \par \par \uc2 Reserve Bank Governor Alan Bollard said the bank wouldn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to try and influence the "long-run" \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar exchange rate.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  through selling or buying the \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar would only become an option when the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is "exceptionally and unjustifiably" high or low, he said.  \par \par \uc2 "By unjustifiable, we mean when the exchange rate has moved to a level in excess of that readily explained by the relevant economic fundamentals, which occurs only infrequently," Bollard said in a statement. "This process is similar to that used for some years by the Reserve Bank of Australia."  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's current policy is to use \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  only if the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets became "disorderly."  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  Dollar Dives  \par \par \uc2 Jason Wong, chief economist at First NZ Capital, said the change in policy isn't surprising given Cullen's recent hints, and added it will bring New Zealand into line with the way central banks in other countries operate in their \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets.  \par \par \uc2 John Body, senior dealer at ANZ Bank, said Bollard's statements in fact "water down" Cullen's recent \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rhetoric.  \par \par \uc2 The Reserve Bank is unlikely to fight the trend of the New Zealand dollar either on its way up or down, but simply \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  toward the perceived end of a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  cycle to hasten a rise or fall.  \par \par \uc2 Nonetheless, the New Zealand dollar, or Kiwi as it is colloquially known, took a severe beating Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 Part of the reason for the sharp fall was attributed by dealers to the Reserve Bank's decision, also announced Thursday, to leave its Official Cash Rate unchanged at 5.25%.  \par \par \uc2 A wafer-thin majority had expected the cash rate to be raised a quarter percentage point to 5.5% following January's surprise increase.  \par \par \uc2 The Kiwi slipped 1.9% to US$0.6558 from US$0.6685 before the rate and \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  announcements. It is now around US$0.6590.  \par \par \uc2 The threat of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  "has really spooked the market," said a dealer. "Exporters feel as though Cullen has just underwritten them."  \par \par \uc2 New Zealand's main opposition National party attacked the shift to \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 It will "prove to be about as effective as a pop gun in a bank robbery," said the party's associate finance spokesman John Key. "As much as we all have sympathy for the current plight of exporters, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is the equivalent of a financial mirage," he said.  \par \par \uc2 Bollard also said having the ability to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  would help the bank to maintain annual consumer price inflation within its 1% to 3% target range, by avoiding unnecessary "instability in output, interest rates and the exchange rate."  \par \par \uc2 He acknowledged that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  could only induce small changes in the exchange rate at the "extremes of its cycles."  \par \par \uc2 Bollard also said "there could be financial risks to the bank" in \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but didn't elaborate on what those risks were.  \par \par \uc2 "There is more work and consultation to be done before final decisions can be made or the setting of \b \highlight22\uc2 operational\b0 \highlight\uc2  procedures and capacities."  \par \par \uc2 -By Shri Navaratnam and Stephen Wright, Dow Jones Newswires; 64-4-471-5990; shri.navaratnam@dowjones.com [ 11-03-04 0202GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020040311e03b0002h\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
