\par\par \b \uc2 NZ dollar still under pressure after sell-off.  \b0\par\par\uc2 518 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2004\par 23:46\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 WELLINGTON, March 12 (Reuters) - The New Zealand dollar was trading off its lows but was still very weak on Friday with a bombing in Spain and renewed fears of another terror attack on the United States heightening already extreme volatility.  \par \par \uc2 The kiwi had sunk well below key support overnight to $0.6420, where it met with keen exporter interest.  \par \par \uc2 By 11:10 a.m. (2210 GMT) the kiwi was at $0.6449/59, still down a cent from $0.6560/70 late on Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 Thursday's announcement from the Reserve Bank of NZ that it would leave interest rates unchanged at 5.25 percent and dovish comments accompanying the statement surprised some in the market, leading to selling pressure that persisted throughout the day.  \par \par \uc2 Opinion had been divided on whether the bank would move rates or not, but a slight majority favoured a rate hike.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also said it wanted the capacity to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to influence the level of the New Zealand dollar.  \par \par \uc2 "A lot of people thought they would hike rates and the statement on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  also had a negative impact on the \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar," said Justin McCarthy, senior economist at Westpac.  \par \par \uc2 In Australia, surprisingly soft jobs data has got the market questioning whether Australia will be able to raise rates again.  \par \par \uc2 Reserve Bank governor Alan Bollard reiterated on Friday that the bank was not necessarily looking to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 "We are seeking a capacity to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 . We are not necessarily looking to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  or certainly not in the near future...It may well never happen," Bollard told Radio NZ.  \par \par \uc2 The bank's proposal had the immediate support of Finance Minister Michael Cullen.  \par \par \uc2 "If you can achieve your desired end simply by wielding the stick, why bother with the messy business of actually using it," Johnathan Bayley, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Westpac Institutional Bank, said in a commentary.  \par \par \uc2 "With the New Zealand/US dollar down by 200 points in 24 hours and down more than 600 points from its February high, Dr Cullen must be pleased with the impact the threat alone is having," Bayley said.  \par \par \uc2 The kiwi's move through the critical level of $0.6520 may signal an end to the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's uptrend, with market expected to be nervous in near term, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 Data showing merchandise terms of trade rose 2.5 percent in the fourth quarter from the previous quarter, had little immediate impact.  \par \par \uc2 Economists polled by Reuters forecast the terms of trade to rise 1.2 percent on the previous quarter and by 4.6 percent on the same quarter a year ago.  \par \par \uc2 Bonds were stronger in line with a surge in U.S. Treasuries after renewed fears of another terror attack from Osama bin Laden's militant Islamic al Qaeda network.  \par \par \uc2 Among the movements, February 2005 bonds were at 5.30 percent, down four basis points from Thursday's close.  \par \par \uc2 November 2006s were at 5.31 percent, July 2009s at 5.48 percent, and April 2013s were at 5.62 percent, all down eight basis points.   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040311e03b0039j\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
