\par\par \b \uc2 Australian, NZ dollars hit this year's lows vs US$.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Christina Fincher  \par \uc2 415 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2004\par 12:53\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 LONDON, March 11 (Reuters) - The Australian and New Zealand dollars crumbled to this year's lows against the greenback on Thursday as investors scaled back bets on further interest rate rises.  \par \par \uc2 Dovish comments from New Zealand's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and a surprisingly weak Australian jobs report were the catalysts for the move, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 The New Zealand dollar tumbled as much as two percent to US$0.6460 , staging one of its biggest one-day slides of recent years. The Australian dollar was not far behind, sliding 1.75 percent to US$0.7341 . Both \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were just off session lows at 1140 GMT.  \par \par \uc2 New Zealand's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  left its benchmark interest rate unchanged on Thursday, confounding many in the market who had expected it to raise rates for the second time this year.  \par \par \uc2 It also said it wanted the capacity to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to influence the level of the New Zealand dollar.  \par \par \uc2 "A lot of people thought they would hike rates and the statement on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  also had a negative impact on the \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar," said Justin McCarthy, senior economist at Westpac.  \par \par \uc2 "In Australia, surprisingly soft jobs data has got the market questioning whether Australia will be able to raise rates again."  \par \par \uc2 TIDE TURNING?  \par \par \uc2 Australia's jobless rate edged up to 5.9 percent in February reflecting the first loss in full-time jobs in eight months.  \par \par \uc2 The figures surprised the market which took the view that Australia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would keep rates on hold for a fourth consecutive month in April.  \par \par \uc2 Both the Australian and New Zealand dollars rallied sharply at the start of the year as investors grew increasingly bearish on the dollar and piled into \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  with high or rising interest rates.  \par \par \uc2 Driven by a thirst for yield as U.S. interest rates languished at four-decade lows, carry trades - borrowing in a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  with low interest rates to invest in high-yielding - have been a key driver of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  over the past two years.  \par \par \uc2 At 5.25 percent, interest rates in Australia and New Zealand remain the highest in the industrialised world, but analysts are now doubtful how much higher they will go. "We are seeing a general unwinding of carry trades," said Adam Cole, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Credit Agrocole Indosuez.  \par \par \uc2 "This is why we are seeing such a sharp pullback in the Aussie and New Zealand dollars today."   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040311e03b001r0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
