\par\par \b \uc2 NZD down 2pct, bonds firm as RBNZ talks  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 .  \b0\par\par\uc2 446 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2004\par 06:13\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2  WELLINGTON, March 11 (Reuters) - The \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar  settled nearly two percent lower on Thursday after the Reserve Bank of New Zealand left rates unchanged and sought government approval for \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2  The kiwi fell 1.9 percent towards the mid-65 cent level following the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's announcement, compounding a fall of around one percent in offshore trading before the announcement.   \par \par \uc2  The bank's statement on formal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , released alongside its decision to leave its benchmark interest rate steady at 5.25 percent, put the skids under the kiwi.   \par \par \uc2  Markets had narrowly predicted a 25 basis point rate hike, and economists polled after the decision were evenly split between no change and a 25 basis point rise at the April rate review.   \par \par \uc2  By 6:00 p.m. (0500 GMT) the kiwi was at $0.6568/75 against $0.6734/44 late on Wednesday.   \par \par \uc2  "On the kneejerk reaction (to the rate announcement) it would have been down about 40 pips and when the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  talk hit the wires it lost another 40 again, so it definitely exacerbated it," Westpac senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist Johnathan Bayley said.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The kiwi also weakened against other key \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , losing 0.8 percent\par against the Australian dollar  and nearly two percent against the euro\par         .\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par While New Zealand remained attractive on yield, offering the highest\par rates in the developed world along with Australia, it could not offer\par the prospect of growth that other economies did, Jon Clarke of Bancorp\par Treasury Service.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par He said the fall in the kiwi came against a backdrop of volatility in\par the global markets, and uncertainty about the U.S. dollar's continued\par decline.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "The market is looking away a little bit from yield to growth outlook,"\par Clarke said.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The RBNZ comment it should have the capacity to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market was "a slightly more aggressive comment on that than\par the markets probably thought."\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The kiwi was on track to test the year's low of $0.6520, which would\par leave the way open for a fall towards 64 cents.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "The market probably needs to regain something above 67 cents or\par $0.6750 before it would be comfortable again," Clarke said.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Bonds, which rallied sharply after the bank's statement, saw little\par activity in the afternoon with the effects of weaker than expected\par Australian employment data the dominant force on the New Zealand\par market.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "If anything the long end's under a wee bit of pressure, the short end\par no-one's really getting amongst it at the moment, no-one knows how to\par interpret the comments on the dollar at the moment," the dealer said.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040311e03b000nn\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
