\par\par \b \uc2 WRAPUP 1-RBNZ holds rates, wants  \highlight22\uc2 forex intervention \highlight\uc2  power.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Gyles Beckford  \par \uc2 780 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2004\par 05:29\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 WELLINGTON, March 11 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  kept interest rates steady on Thursday and signalled it might act to rein in the country's high-flying \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , reflecting concern about making monetary policy too restrictive.  \par \par \uc2 The Reserve Bank of New Zealand (RBNZ) left its official cash rate at 5.25 percent, saying it would watch for signs of economic cooling before deciding if another small tightening was needed. New Zealand's rates are among the highest in the developed world.  \par \par \uc2 But the RBNZ took the unusual step of saying it would ask the government for power to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. Since the kiwi was floated in 1985, the RBNZ has never \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Even after a fall of about seven percent against the U.S. dollar over the past few weeks, the New Zealand dollar has risen some 55 percent in a little more than two years, fuelled by a booming economy.  \par \par \uc2 The RBNZ is worried another rate rise now - after January's surprise quarter-point move and coupled with the effects of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strength - might exacerbate an economic slowdown, when it eventually comes.  \par \par \uc2 But New Zealand's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves are paltry and the RBNZ governor himself, Alan Bollard, said the country's ability to influence the market was limited.  \par \par \uc2 "At best, we can influence the exchange rate only by small amounts at the extremes of its cycle when it is a long way from economic fundamentals," Bollard said.  \par \par \uc2 Analysts said the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  move might not be taken seriously.  \par \par \uc2 "He's on a fool's errand," said Brendan O'Donovan, chief economist at Westpac, referring to Bollard. "It would be completely ineffective. Our pockets aren't deep enough to have any influence."  \par \par \uc2 New Zealand's foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves are NZ$3.5 billion (US$2.3 billion). That is a tiny fraction of the hundreds of billions of dollars held by many Asian central banks, which have been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to restrain their own \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and protect export markets.  \par \par \uc2 TAMING THE KIWI  \par \par \uc2 The RBNZ already has the power to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  when markets become "disorderly". Bollard said he would ask the government for the capacity to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  when the \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar reached "exceptional and unjustifiable" levels.  \par \par \uc2 The RBNZ said it envisaged acting only when the kiwi moved to a level in "excess of that readily explained by the relevant economic fundamentals".  \par \par \uc2 Finance Minister Michael Cullen embraced the RBNZ plan.  \par \par \uc2 "I am strongly supportive of the change and will be recommending it to my ministerial colleagues," Cullen said.  \par \par \uc2 A spokeswoman for Cullen said a law change was not needed for the RBNZ to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but approval from a majority in parliament was necessary.  \par \par \uc2 The kiwi was trading around $0.6680 just before the rate and \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  news. It lost more than three quarters of a U.S. cent immediately on the announcement and was last at $0.6562, down nearly two percent from before the news.  \par \par \uc2 Bank-bill futures and short-dated bonds rallied, with the 90-day bank bill yield falling 15 basis points.  \par \par \uc2 The bank said that on a trade-weighted basis the New Zealand dollar was about 15 percent above its long-term average, and some exporters had been through "considerable pain" because of its strength.  \par \par \uc2 New Zealand's agriculture-dominated exports make up about one third of gross domestic product.  \par \par \uc2 BALANCING ACT  \par \par \uc2 The RBNZ said it was balancing indicators showing a robust domestic economy against an expected slowdown. Immigration, a driver of recent growth, is expected to ease and booming housing and property markets are thought to be cooling.  \par \par \uc2 "With this uncertainty we judge it as appropriate at this stage to wait and watch the data, to see whether a further small increase in interest rates will be required this year," it said.  \par \par \uc2 The bank said inflation would rise to the top of a target range of one to three-percent over the coming year. Economic growth was set to halve to 1.75 percent in the year to March 2005 from current levels.  \par \par \uc2 "The projected growth slowdown is due mainly to the lagged effects of the high New Zealand dollar and an expected slowdown in population growth," it said.  \par \par \uc2 Economists said a wait-and-see approach seemed appropriate.  \par \par \uc2 "My suspicion is, now that they've done nothing, that as time passes more evidence of the economy slowing will emerge and the need for tightening will become less and less," said UBS New Zealand chief economist Robin Clements.  \par \par \uc2 A Reuters poll of economists taken after the decision put the odds between a rate rise in April against no change at 50-50.   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040311e03b000jp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
