\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-NZ  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  seeks power to  \highlight22\uc2 intervene \highlight\uc2  in NZD.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By James Gray  \par \uc2 543 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2004\par 01:42\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 WELLINGTON, March 11 (Reuters) - The Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Thursday it wanted the capacity to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to influence the level of the \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar.  \par \par \uc2 The Reserve Bank's current policy is to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  only if the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market becomes "disorderly", but it has never done so since the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was floated in early 1985.  \par \par \uc2 The bank's statement, released alongside its decision to leave its benchmark interest rate unchanged at 5.25 percent, put the skids under an already weak New Zealand dollar.  \par \par \uc2 "On the kneejerk reaction (to the rate announcement) it would have been down about 40 pips and when the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  talk hit the wires it lost another 40 again, so it definitely exacerbated it," Westpac senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist Johnathan Bayley said.  \par \par \uc2 By 1:10 p.m. (0010 GMT) the kiwi was at $0.6595/03 against $0.6675/85 before the announcement.  \par \par \uc2 The NZ dollar has been one of the best performing \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the past year rising around 20 percent against the U.S. dollar. The RBNZ estimated the trade weighted New Zealand dollar was around 15 percent above its long-term average.  \par \par \uc2 The kiwi's rise has been largely driven by the decline in the U.S. dollar but also by high interest rates.  \par \par \uc2 Finance Minister Michael Cullen, who had previously floated the idea of such \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , quickly backed the RBNZ proposal.  \par \par \uc2 "I am strongly supportive of the change and will be recommending it to my ministerial colleagues," Cullen said.  \par \par \uc2 DEVIL IN THE DETAIL  \par \par \uc2 Economists said the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  plan raised issues and needed to be fleshed out.  \par \par \uc2 "Our concern is the RBNZ needs a better \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (\b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) forecasting process in order to assess what "justifiable" NZ dollar levels are," said Citigroup's director of economic and market analysis, Annette Beacher.  \par \par \uc2 Bollard said the bank envisaged operating as in a similar way to its Australian counterpart, allowing it to sell the kiwi to put downward pressure on the exchange rate, or buy to exert upward pressure.  \par \par \uc2 The bank would look at \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  when the \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar reached "exceptional and unjustifiable levels" beyond what could be explained by economic fundamentals.  \par \par \uc2 The general aim would be to influence the exchange rate in a way consistent with maintaining price stability and that the bank would not seek to change the long-run exchange rate, he said.  \par \par \uc2 "At best, we can influence the exchange rate only by a small amounts at the extremes of its cycle when it is a long way from economic fundamentals," he said.  \par \par \uc2 However, Westpac chief economist Brendan O'Donovan, doubted the RBNZ, with \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves currently around NZ$3.5 billion ($2.3 billion), could make any difference.  \par \par \uc2 "He's (Bollard) on a fool's errand. It would be completely ineffective," he said.  \par \par \uc2 "Our pockets aren't deep enough to have any influence, if you've put your hand up, you've set yourself as a target, you'll be run over."  \par \par \uc2 A spokeswoman for Cullen said a law change would not be needed to empower the RBNZ to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but the backing of a majority in parliament would be needed.   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040311e03b0003d\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
