\par\par \b \uc2 NZ Fin Min: Strongly Supportive Of Change In  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  Policy  \b0\par\par\uc2 193 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2004\par 21:38\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 WELLINGTON (Dow Jones)--New Zealand Finance Minister Michael Cullen said Thursday he is "strongly supportive" of a proposal for the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to take a more active role in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.  \par \par \uc2 The Reserve Bank of New Zealand earlier Thursday said it has asked Cullen to be allowed to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to influence the \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar when it is unjustifiably low or high.  \par \par \uc2 Cullen said in a statement that a Cabinet paper incorporating the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's advise is being drafted and will be presented to the Cabinet of government ministers in the near future.  \par \par \uc2 "As anyone who has been following my statements on monetary policy management over recent months will know, I am strongly supportive of the change and will be recommending it to my ministerial colleagues," he said.  \par \par \uc2 Cullen said he will be consulting with other political parties to achieve a parliamentary majority for the change in policy, which will require a motion in parliament.  \par \par \uc2 -Wellington Bureau, Dow Jones Newswires; 64-4-471-5990; djnews.wellington@dowjones.com [ 10-03-04 2046GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020040310e03a00115\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
