\par\par \b \uc2 Text Of NZ  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  Statement On  \highlight22\uc2 FX Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 435 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2004\par 21:09\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 Following is the verbatim text of Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 New Zealand\b0 \highlight\uc2 's statement on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Capacity to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market proposed  \par \par \uc2 The Reserve Bank has provided advice to the Minister of Finance recommending that, as one of its monetary policy implementation tools, it should have the capacity to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to influence the level of the exchange rate.  \par \par \uc2 The Reserve Bank's current stance is to use its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  only if the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market became "disorderly".  \par \par \uc2 Reserve Bank Governor Alan Bollard said "We have recommended that when the New Zealand dollar is exceptionally and unjustifiably high, the Reserve Bank would be able to use New Zealand dollars to buy \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which would put downward pressure on the exchange rate.  \par \par \uc2 "And, when the exchange rate is exceptionally and unjustifiably low, we would be able to sell \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy New Zealand dollars, putting upwards pressure on the exchange rate.  \par \par \uc2 "By unjustifiable, we mean when the exchange rate has moved to a level in excess of that readily explained by the relevant economic fundamentals, which occurs only infrequently. This process is similar to that used for some years by the Reserve Bank of Australia.  \par \par \uc2 "By having this \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  tool, we would generally aim to influence the exchange rate in a direction consistent with maintaining our price stability goal.  \par \par \uc2 "The addition of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  as an instrument of monetary policy would also better enable the Bank to meet its Policy Targets Agreement clause 4B commitment, which stipulates that "In pursuing its price stability objective, the Bank shall seek to avoid unnecessary instability in output, interest rates and the exchange rate." That is, at extreme levels of the exchange rate, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  may be chosen to supplement monetary policy.  \par \par \uc2 "Importantly, such \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would not be trying to permanently change the long-run exchange rate. And, the New Zealand dollar exchange rate cycle would not be eliminated.  \par \par \uc2 "At best, we can influence the exchange rate only by small amounts at the extremes of its cycle when it is a long way from economic fundamentals. In doing this there could be financial risks to the Bank, requiring very careful management.  \par \par \uc2 "In recent days we have put these ideas to the Minister of Finance. There is more work and consultation to be done before final decisions can be made or the setting of \b \highlight22\uc2 operational\b0 \highlight\uc2  procedures and capacities," Dr Bollard concluded.  \par \par \uc2 -Wellington Bureau, Dow Jones Newswires; 64-4-471-5990; djnews.wellington@dowjones.com [ 10-03-04 2009GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020040310e03a00109\par }\par \b \uc2 Zusammenfassung der Suche\b0\par \par  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\b